intactivity-sharepoint-activity-per-user-per-date)\n+  - [`ms365_copilot_usage` — Copilot AI usage per user per date](#ms365copilotusage-copilot-ai-usage-per-user-per-date)\n+  - [`ms365_collection_runs` — Connector execution log](#ms365collectionruns-connector-execution-log)\n+- [Identity Resolution](#identity-resolution)\n+- [Silver / Gold Mappings](#silver-gold-mappings)\n+- [Open Questions](#open-questions)\n+  - [OQ-M365-1: Copilot endpoint availability and schema](#oq-m365-1-copilot-endpoint-availability-and-schema)\n+  - [OQ-M365-2: OneDrive and SharePoint Silver mapping](#oq-m365-2-onedrive-and-sharepoint-silver-mapping)\n+\n+<!-- /toc -->\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Overview\n+\n+**API**: Microsoft Graph API v1.0 — Report endpoints (`/reports/get*ActivityUserDetail`)\n+\n+**Category**: Communication\n+\n+**Identity**: `userPrincipalName` (UPN, email address) — resolved to canonical `person_id` via Identity Manager\n+\n+**Field naming**: camelCase — original Graph API field names, no renaming at Bronze level.\n+\n+**Why six tables**: The Graph API exposes Email, Teams, OneDrive, SharePoint, and Copilot activity as separate endpoints with different report periods and field sets. Each is stored as its own Bronze table sharing the same identity key (`userPrincipalName + reportRefreshDate`). The collection run log is a seventh monitoring-only table.","path":"docs/connectors/m365.md","commit_id":"bcf3409acfe00fdacb837fe2669cd1ff743698f2","original_commit_id":"125d535e176539614fa872ed4fb3f46e76c2fa1e","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Resolve table-count inconsistency in Overview.**\n\n**Line 38** says “Why six tables” but the same sentence states the collection run log is a **seventh** table. Please make the count wording consistent.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Suggested wording</summary>\n\n```diff\n-**Why six tables**: The Graph API exposes Email, Teams, OneDrive, SharePoint, and Copilot activity as separate endpoints with different report periods and field sets. Each is stored as its own Bronze table sharing the same identity key (`userPrincipalName + reportRefreshDate`). The collection run log is a seventh monitoring-only table.\n+**Why seven tables**: The Graph API exposes Email, Teams, OneDrive, SharePoint, and Copilot activity as separate endpoints with different report periods and field sets. Each is stored as its own Bronze table sharing the same identity key (`userPrincipalName + reportRefreshDate`). `ms365_collection_runs` is a seventh monitoring-only table.\n```\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Committable suggestion</summary>\n\n> ‼️ **IMPORTANT**\n> Carefully review the code before committing. Ensure that it accurately replaces the highlighted code, contains no missing lines, and has no issues with indentation. Thoroughly test & benchmark the code to ensure it meets the requirements.\n\n```suggestion\n**Why seven tables**: The Graph API exposes Email, Teams, OneDrive, SharePoint, and Copilot activity as separate endpoints with different report periods and field sets. Each is stored as its own Bronze table sharing the same identity key (`userPrincipalName + reportRefreshDate`). `ms365_collection_runs` is a seventh monitoring-only table.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_end -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@docs/connectors/m365.md` at line 38, Update the phrasing around “Why six\ntables” to be consistent with the rest of the sentence: either change the\nheading text to “Why seven tables” or reword the sentence to “Why six data\ntables and a seventh collection run log (monitoring-only) table” so the count\nmatches; locate the phrase “Why six tables” and the clause mentioning “The\ncollection run log is a seventh monitoring-only table” in\ndocs/connectors/m365.md and apply the chosen wording change.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:triton:hawk -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-03-04T19:00:35Z","updated_at":"2026-03-04T19:00:38Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/5#discussion_r2885525401","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/5","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/2885525401"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/5#discussion_r2885525401"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/5"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/2885525401/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":38,"original_line":38,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"NONE","original_position":38,"position":38,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/2885525408","pull_request_review_id":3891359811,"id":2885525408,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDORRWv8s6r_Z-g","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,145 @@\n+# OpenAI API Connector Specification\n+\n+> Version 1.0 — March 2026\n+> Based on: `docs/CONNECTORS_REFERENCE.md` Source 18 (OpenAI API), OQ-3\n+\n+Standalone specification for the OpenAI API (AI Tool) connector. Expands Source 18 in the main Connector Reference with full table schemas, identity mapping, Silver/Gold pipeline notes, and open questions.\n+\n+<!-- toc -->\n+\n+- [Overview](#overview)\n+- [Bronze Tables](#bronze-tables)\n+  - [`openai_api_daily_usage` — Daily token usage per API key per model](#openaiapidailyusage-daily-token-usage-per-api-key-per-model)\n+  - [`openai_api_requests` — Individual API request events](#openaiapirequests-individual-api-request-events)\n+  - [`openai_api_collection_runs` — Connector execution log](#openaiapicollectionruns-connector-execution-log)\n+- [Identity Resolution](#identity-resolution)\n+- [Silver / Gold Mappings](#silver-gold-mappings)\n+- [Open Questions](#open-questions)\n+  - [OQ-OAPI-1: `reasoning_tokens` for o1/o3 — cost accounting in Silver](#oq-oapi-1-reasoningtokens-for-o1o3-cost-accounting-in-silver)\n+  - [OQ-OAPI-2: Parallel to Claude API — unified Silver stream?](#oq-oapi-2-parallel-to-claude-api-unified-silver-stream)\n+","path":"docs/connectors/openai-api.md","commit_id":"bcf3409acfe00fdacb837fe2669cd1ff743698f2","original_commit_id":"125d535e176539614fa872ed4fb3f46e76c2fa1e","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Fix broken TOC anchor fragments.**\n\nOn Line 12 through Line 20, the fragment IDs don’t match the heading anchor style for code-formatted names (e.g., `openai_api_daily_usage`), so links are likely non-functional in rendered docs.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@docs/connectors/openai-api.md` around lines 12 - 20, TOC links use\ncode-formatted names that don't match generated heading anchors; update the\nanchor fragments so they match the rendered heading IDs for the code-style\nheadings (e.g., openai_api_daily_usage, openai_api_requests,\nopenai_api_collection_runs, Identity Resolution, Silver / Gold Mappings, Open\nQuestions, and the OQ items). Edit the TOC entries in the OpenAI connector doc\nto remove backticks or change fragments to the exact heading anchor format\nproduced by the markdown renderer (match headings for openai_api_daily_usage,\nopenai_api_requests, openai_api_collection_runs and the OQ anchors like\noq-oapi-1 and oq-oapi-2) so the links resolve correctly.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:triton:hawk -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-03-04T19:00:35Z","updated_at":"2026-03-04T19:00:38Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/5#discussion_r2885525408","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/5","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/2885525408"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/5#discussion_r2885525408"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/5"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/2885525408/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":12,"original_start_line":12,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":20,"original_line":20,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"NONE","original_position":20,"position":20,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/2885525411","pull_request_review_id":3891359811,"id":2885525411,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDORRWv8s6r_Z-j","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,145 @@\n+# OpenAI API Connector Specification\n+\n+> Version 1.0 — March 2026\n+> Based on: `docs/CONNECTORS_REFERENCE.md` Source 18 (OpenAI API), OQ-3\n+\n+Standalone specification for the OpenAI API (AI Tool) connector. Expands Source 18 in the main Connector Reference with full table schemas, identity mapping, Silver/Gold pipeline notes, and open questions.\n+\n+<!-- toc -->\n+\n+- [Overview](#overview)\n+- [Bronze Tables](#bronze-tables)\n+  - [`openai_api_daily_usage` — Daily token usage per API key per model](#openaiapidailyusage-daily-token-usage-per-api-key-per-model)\n+  - [`openai_api_requests` — Individual API request events](#openaiapirequests-individual-api-request-events)\n+  - [`openai_api_collection_runs` — Connector execution log](#openaiapicollectionruns-connector-execution-log)\n+- [Identity Resolution](#identity-resolution)\n+- [Silver / Gold Mappings](#silver-gold-mappings)\n+- [Open Questions](#open-questions)\n+  - [OQ-OAPI-1: `reasoning_tokens` for o1/o3 — cost accounting in Silver](#oq-oapi-1-reasoningtokens-for-o1o3-cost-accounting-in-silver)\n+  - [OQ-OAPI-2: Parallel to Claude API — unified Silver stream?](#oq-oapi-2-parallel-to-claude-api-unified-silver-stream)\n+\n+<!-- /toc -->\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Overview\n+\n+**API**: OpenAI Usage API (`/v1/usage`)\n+\n+**Category**: AI Tool\n+\n+**Authentication**: Admin API key (OpenAI Platform)\n+\n+**Identity**: `user_id` in `openai_api_requests` — the value of the `user` field in the request body, set by the caller. Nullable — attribution is only possible when the calling application includes this field. `openai_api_daily_usage` has no user-level attribution.\n+\n+**Field naming**: snake_case — preserved as-is at Bronze level.\n+\n+**Why two tables**: Same pattern as Claude API (Source 13) — daily aggregates (always available) and per-request events (require caller instrumentation). The `user` field in OpenAI requests is a caller convention, not enforced.\n+\n+**Parallel to Claude API**: This connector mirrors the Claude API connector structure. The main OpenAI-specific difference is `reasoning_tokens` — an internal thinking token count specific to reasoning models (o1, o3) that are billed but not visible in the response.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Bronze Tables\n+\n+### `openai_api_daily_usage` — Daily token usage per API key per model\n+\n+| Field | Type | Description |\n+|-------|------|-------------|\n+| `date` | date | Usage date |\n+| `api_key_id` | text | API key identifier (name or last-4 alias) |\n+| `model` | text | Model ID, e.g. `gpt-4o`, `gpt-4o-mini`, `o1`, `o3-mini` |\n+| `request_count` | numeric | Number of API requests |\n+| `input_tokens` | numeric | Input (prompt) tokens consumed |\n+| `output_tokens` | numeric | Output (completion) tokens generated |\n+| `cached_tokens` | numeric | Tokens served from prompt cache |\n+| `reasoning_tokens` | numeric | Internal reasoning tokens (o1/o3 models only; billed but not in output) |\n+| `total_cost_cents` | numeric | Total cost in cents |\n+\n+Granularity: one row per `(date, api_key_id, model)`. `reasoning_tokens` is zero for non-reasoning models.\n+\n+---\n+\n+### `openai_api_requests` — Individual API request events\n+\n+Available when the caller passes a `user` field in the request body. Without this field, requests are not recorded at this level.\n+\n+| Field | Type | Description |\n+|-------|------|-------------|\n+| `request_id` | text | Unique request ID from response headers |\n+| `timestamp` | timestamptz | Request timestamp |\n+| `api_key_id` | text | API key used |\n+| `user_id` | text | Value of `user` field in the request body — caller-defined identifier (nullable) |\n+| `model` | text | Model ID |","path":"docs/connectors/openai-api.md","commit_id":"bcf3409acfe00fdacb837fe2669cd1ff743698f2","original_commit_id":"125d535e176539614fa872ed4fb3f46e76c2fa1e","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Resolve contradiction in request-level availability semantics.**\n\nLine 65 says requests are not recorded without `user`, but Line 72 defines `user_id` as nullable. These two statements conflict and can mislead implementers about whether records exist with `NULL user_id`.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@docs/connectors/openai-api.md` around lines 65 - 73, The documentation\ncontradicts itself about request-level recording: either requests are only\nrecorded when the request body includes a `user` field, or requests are always\nrecorded and `user_id` can be NULL; pick one and make the text consistent.\nUpdate the sentence that currently reads \"Available when the caller passes a\n`user` field...\" and the `user_id` column description so they match: if you\nintend to always record requests, change the sentence to state requests are\nrecorded and `user_id` is nullable when the `user` field is omitted; if you\nintend to record only when `user` is present, mark `user_id` as non-nullable and\nstate that rows are only created when `user` is provided. Ensure both the\nexplanatory sentence and the `user_id` table entry use the same policy (`user`\nvs `user_id`) so implementers are not misled.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:triton:hawk -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-03-04T19:00:35Z","updated_at":"2026-03-04T19:00:38Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/5#discussion_r2885525411","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/5","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/2885525411"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/5#discussi