blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧹 Nitpick comments (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>docs/connectors/cursor.md (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`48-48`: **Consider renaming `unique` field to avoid SQL reserved keyword.**\n\nThe field name `unique` is a SQL reserved keyword, which may require quoting in queries and could cause issues with some database tools or ORMs. Consider renaming to `unique_id`, `record_id`, or `primary_key`.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>Suggested alternative names</summary>\n\n```diff\n-| `unique` | text | Primary key |\n+| `unique_id` | text | Primary key |\n```\n\nOr:\n```diff\n-| `unique` | text | Primary key |\n+| `event_id` | text | Primary key |\n```\n\nThis same field appears in both `cursor_daily_usage` (line 48) and `cursor_events` (line 82).\n</details>\n\n\nAlso applies to: 82-82\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@docs/connectors/cursor.md` at line 48, Rename the SQL column currently named\n`unique` in both `cursor_daily_usage` and `cursor_events` to a non-reserved\nidentifier (suggest `unique_id` or `record_id`); update the schema definitions,\nany CREATE/ALTER migration scripts, all SELECT/INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE queries, ORM\nmodel mappings, and documentation references (`cursor_daily_usage` and\n`cursor_events`) to use the new name; ensure any code that quoted the column is\nadjusted and add a migration that backfills/renames the column to preserve data\nand maintain backwards compatibility.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for all review comments with AI agents</summary>\n\n````\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nInline comments:\nIn `@docs/connectors/allure.md`:\n- Around line 12-20: The TOC entries using code-formatted headings (e.g.,\n`allure_launches`, `allure_test_results`, `allure_defects`,\n`allure_collection_runs`, \"Identity Resolution\", \"Silver / Gold Mappings\", \"Open\nQuestions\" and the OQ entries like OQ-AL-1/OQ-AL-2) have incorrect fragment IDs;\nupdate each TOC link to match the actual generated heading IDs by removing\ninline code formatting and converting the displayed headings to their real slug\nform (normalize to lowercase, replace spaces and slashes with hyphens, strip\npunctuation) so the links point to the real anchors in the document.\n\nIn `@docs/connectors/bitbucket.md`:\n- Around line 12-21: The TOC fragment links don’t match the generated heading\nIDs; update each link to the GitHub-style/sluggified heading ID (lowercase,\nspaces and punctuation replaced with hyphens) so the anchors point to actual\nheadings: change bitbucket_repositories → bitbucket-repositories,\nbitbucket_branches → bitbucket-branches, bitbucket_commits → bitbucket-commits,\nbitbucket_commit_files — Per-file line changes →\nbitbucket-commit-files-per-file-line-changes, bitbucket_pull_requests →\nbitbucket-pull-requests, bitbucket_pull_request_reviewers — Reviewer list with\nstatus → bitbucket-pull-request-reviewers-reviewer-list-with-status,\nbitbucket_pull_request_comments → bitbucket-pull-request-comments,\nbitbucket_pull_request_commits → bitbucket-pull-request-commits,\nbitbucket_ticket_refs — Ticket references extracted from PRs and commits →\nbitbucket-ticket-refs-ticket-references-extracted-from-prs-and-commits, and\nbitbucket_collection_runs — Connector execution log →\nbitbucket-collection-runs-connector-execution-log (or regenerate the TOC using\nyour markdown processor/markdownlint fix to ensure exact anchors).\n\nIn `@docs/connectors/claude-api.md`:\n- Around line 12-14: The TOC links for the three Bronze tables use incorrect\nfragment IDs; update the three anchor fragments so they match the actual\ngenerated heading anchors for the backticked table names\n(`claude_api_daily_usage`, `claude_api_requests`, `claude_