emselves (e.g., via a custom\nheader or pattern) and explicitly state that `X-Anthropic-User-Id` maps only to\n`user_id` (leave `user_id` mapping unchanged) — ensure references to\n`application`, `X-Anthropic-User-Id`, and `user_id` are clarified and not\nmerged.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n---\n\n`494-494`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**`zulip_users.role` is missing moderator (`300`) in the enum description.**\n\nLine 494 currently skips moderator, which can cause downstream role filters to be wrong.\n\n  \n\n<details>\n<summary>🔧 Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-| `role` | numeric | 100 owner / 200 admin / 400 member / 600 guest |\n+| `role` | numeric | 100 owner / 200 admin / 300 moderator / 400 member / 600 guest |\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@docs/CONNECTORS_REFERENCE.md` at line 494, The docs entry for\nzulip_users.role omits the moderator value; update the enum description in\nCONNECTORS_REFERENCE.md for `zulip_users.role` to include moderator (numeric\nvalue 300) between admin (200) and member (400), e.g., list: 100 owner / 200\nadmin / 300 moderator / 400 member / 600 guest so downstream role filters\nreading `zulip_users.role` will be correct.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n---\n\n`783-783`: _⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**The task↔git join path is documented incorrectly.**\n\nLine 783 suggests matching `task_id` directly against commit message text. The canonical bridge is `*_ticket_refs` (e.g., `github_ticket_refs.external_ticket_id = class_task_tracker.task_id`), then join to commit tables by commit hash/ID.\n\n \n\n<details>\n<summary>🔧 Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-Tasks link to git commits via `task_id` matched against commit messages (extracted ticket pattern).\n+Tasks link to git activity via the `*_ticket_refs` bridge tables — e.g. `github_ticket_refs.external_ticket_id = class_task_tracker.task_id`, then `git