":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"coderabbitai","description":"# Transforming Code Reviews with AI\r\n\r\n## Features\r\n\r\n**Automated Reviews**: Continuous reviews of the pull requests including incremental commits. \r\n\r\n**Summarization**: Generates high-level summary and a technical walkthrough of the PR changes. \r\n\r\n**Line-by-line review**: Provides line-by-line suggestions committable with one click.\r\n\r\n**Codebase verification**:  Verifies the impact on the overall codebase and identifies missing changes.\r\n\r\n**Insights into your code**:  Ask any questions on your codebase within the pull request \r\n\r\n**Chat about your code** : Chat with the bot around your code. The more you chat, the smarter it gets.\r\n\r\n**Issue Validation**:  Validates the PR against the linked issues and identifies other related issues \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n","external_url":"https://coderabbit.ai?utm_source=cr_app&utm_medium=github","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","created_at":"2023-06-14T15:47:27Z","updated_at":"2026-03-14T07:58:44Z","permissions":{"actions":"read","checks":"write","contents":"write","discussions":"read","issues":"write","members":"read","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write","statuses":"write"},"events":["issues","issue_comment","label","organization","pull_request","pull_request_review","pull_request_review_comment","pull_request_review_thread","release","repository"]}}],"source_review_comments":[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/2839934758","pull_request_review_id":3840072782,"id":2839934758,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDORRWv8s6pRfcm","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,267 @@\n+# Table: `cursor_daily_usage`\n+\n+## Overview\n+\n+**Purpose**: Store daily aggregated usage statistics per Cursor IDE user, including feature adoption metrics, code interaction stats, and subscription usage.\n+\n+**Data Source**: Cursor API via Airbyte connector\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Schema Definition\n+\n+| Column | Type | Constraints | Description |\n+|--------|------|-------------|-------------|\n+| `unique` | text | PRIMARY KEY | Unique record identifier |\n+| `day` | text | NOT NULL | Day label |\n+| `date` | bigint | NOT NULL | Unix timestamp in milliseconds |\n+| `email` | text | NOT NULL | User email address |\n+| `userId` | text | NOT NULL | Cursor user ID |","path":"streams/raw_cursor/cursor_daily_usage.md","commit_id":"7b4811e24e84830df73aabdea58e332784a65b32","original_commit_id":"9e1edb2dcc6d5ea476ba219a7577b99ed3772afd","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**PII stored in `email` and `userId` with no compliance note**\n\nSame concern as `cursor_events.userEmail` — `email` is PII and the documentation lacks any retention, access control, or regulatory compliance guidance. Add a Data Privacy note here as well.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@streams/raw_cursor/cursor_daily_usage.md` around lines 18 - 19, The\ndocumentation for the `email` and `userId` columns omits data privacy guidance;\nupdate the cursor_daily_usage documentation to add a Data Privacy note stating\nthat `email` and `userId` are PII, specify retention policy, access controls\n(who/roles can access), encryption/at-rest and in-transit handling, and\napplicable regulatory requirements (e.g., GDPR/CCPA) and links to the central\nprivacy policy; mention any anonymization/pseudonymization options or TTLs for\nthese fields and where to request access.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:triton:churro -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-02-23T09:54:25Z","updated_at":"2026-02-23T09:54:27Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/3#discussion_r2839934758","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/3","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/2839934758"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/3#discussion_r2839934758"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/3"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/2839934758/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":18,"original_start_line":18,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":19,"original_line":19,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"NONE","original_position":19,"position":19,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/2839934772","pull_request_review_id":3840072782,"id":2839934772,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDORRWv8s6pRfc0","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,144 @@\n+# Table: `cursor_events_token_usage`\n+\n+## Overview\n+\n+**Purpose**: Store detailed token consumption metrics for each Cursor IDE event, including input/output tokens, cache usage, and costs.\n+\n+**Data Source**: Cursor API via Airbyte connector\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Schema Definition\n+\n+| Column | Type | Constraints | Description |\n+|--------|------|-------------|-------------|\n+| `event_unique` | text | PRIMARY KEY | Reference to cursor_events.unique |\n+| `totalCents` | numeric | NULLABLE | Total cost in cents |\n+| `inputTokens` | numeric | NULLABLE | Number of input tokens consumed |\n+| `outputTokens` | numeric | NULLABLE | Number of output tokens generated |\n+| `cacheReadTokens` | numeric | NULLABLE | Tokens read from cache |\n+| `cacheWriteTokens` | numeric | NULLABLE | Tokens written to cache |\n+| `discountPercentOff` | numeric | NULLABLE | Discount percentage applied |\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Field Semantics\n+\n+### Core Identifier\n+\n+**`event_unique`** (text, PRIMARY KEY)\n+- **Purpose**: Foreign key linking to the parent event\n+- **References**: `cursor_events.unique`\n+- **Usage**: Join key to event details\n+\n+### Token Metrics\n+\n+**`inputTokens`** (numeric, NULLABLE)\n+- **Purpose**: Number of tokens in the prompt/input\n+- **Format**: Integer count\n+- **Usage**: Understanding prompt complexity, cost attribution\n+\n+**`outputTokens`** (numeric, NULLABLE)\n+- **Purpose**: Number of tokens in the model response\n+- **Format**: Integer count\n+- **Usage**: Response length analysis, cost attribution\n+\n+**`cacheReadTokens`** (numeric, NULLABLE)\n+- **Purpose**: Tokens served from prompt cache\n+- **Format**: Integer count\n+- **Usage**: Cache efficiency analysis, cost savings tracking\n+\n+**`cacheWriteTokens`** (numeric, NULLABLE)\n+- **Purpose**: Tokens written to prompt cache\n+- **Format**: Integer count\n+- **Usage**: Cache utilization tracking\n+\n+### Cost\n+\n+**`totalCents`** (numeric, NULLABLE)\n+- **Purpose**: Total cost for this event in cents\n+- **Format**: Decimal value\n+- **Usage**: Cost tracking, budget analysis\n+\n+**`discountPercentOff`** (numeric, NULLABLE)\n+- **Purpose**: Discount percentage applied to this event\n+- **Format**: Percentage (0-100)\n+- **Usage**: Discount tracking, effective cost calculation\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Relationships\n+\n+### Parent\n+\n+**`cursor_events`**\n+- **Join**: `event_unique` ← `unique`\n+- **Cardinality**: One token usage record to one event\n+- **Description**: Each token usage record belongs to exactly one event\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Usage Examples\n+\n+### Average token usage by model\n+\n+```sql\n+SELECT\n+    e.model,\n+    AVG(t.inputTokens) as avg_input,\n+    AVG(t.outputTokens) as avg_output,\n+    AVG(t.totalCents) as avg_cost_cents\n+FROM cursor_events e\n+JOIN cursor_events_token_usage t ON e.unique = t.event_unique\n+WHERE e.timestamp >= '2026-01-01'\n+GROUP BY e.model\n+ORDER BY avg_cost_cents DESC;\n+```\n+\n+### Cache efficiency\n+\n+```sql\n+SELECT\n+    DATE(e.timestamp) as day,\n+    SUM(t.cacheReadTokens) as cached_tokens,\n+    SUM(t.inputTokens) as total_input_tokens,\n+    ROUND(SUM(t.cacheReadTokens)::numeric / NULLIF(SUM(t.inputTokens), 0) * 100, 2) as cache_hit_pct\n+FROM cursor_events e\n+JOIN cursor_events_token_usage t ON e.unique = t.event_unique\n+WHERE e.timestamp >= NOW() - INTERVAL '30 days'\n+GROUP BY DATE(e.timestamp)\n+ORDER BY day DESC;\n+```\n+\n+### Total spending per user\n+\n+```sql\n+SELECT\n+    e.userEmail,\n+    SUM(t.totalCents) / 100.0 as total_dollars,\n+    SUM(t.inputTokens + t.outputTokens) as total_tokens\n+FROM cursor_events e\n+JOIN cursor_events_token_usage t ON e.unique = t.event_unique\n+WHERE e.timestamp >= '2026-01-01'\n+GROUP BY e.userEmail\n+ORDER BY total_dollars DESC;\n+```","path":"streams/raw_cursor/cursor_events_token_usage.md","commit_id":"7b4811e24e84830df73aabdea58e332784a65b32","original_commit_id":"9e1edb2dcc6d5ea476ba219a7577b99ed3772afd","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**`e.unique` is unquoted in all three JOIN conditions — these queries will fail**\n\nAll three SQL examples reference the `unique` column via `ON e.unique = t.event_unique`. Since `UNIQUE` is a SQL reserved keyword, quoting is required when using PostgreSQL reserved words as identifiers. Running any of these queries as written will produce a syntax error. Every occurrence must be `e.\"unique\"`.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🐛 Proposed fix (applies to lines 92, 107, and 121)</summary>\n\n```diff\n-JOIN cursor_events_token_usage t ON e.unique = t.event_unique\n+JOIN cursor_events_token_usage t ON e.\"unique\" = t.event_unique\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@streams/raw_cursor/cursor_events_token_usage.md` around lines 85 - 125, The\nJOINs use the reserved word identifier e.unique which causes SQL syntax errors;\nupdate all JOIN conditions to quote the unique column (e.\"unique\" =\nt.event_unique) in each query referencing cursor_events and\ncursor_events_token_usage (the three occurrences of e.unique in the SELECTs for\nmodel averages, cache efficiency by day, and total spending per user) so\nPostgreSQL treats it as an identifier rather than the UNIQUE keyword.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:triton:churro -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-02-23T09:54:25Z","updated_at":"2026-02-23T09:54:27Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/3#discussion_r2839934772","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/3","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/2839934772"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/3#discussion_r2839934772"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/3"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/2839934772/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":85,"original_start_line":85,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":125,"original_line":125,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"NONE","original_position":125,"position":125,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/2839934778","pull_request_review_id":3840072782,"id":2839934778,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDORRWv8s6pRfc6","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,173 @@\n+# Table: `cursor_events`\n+\n+## Overview\n+\n+**Purpose**: Store individual Cursor IDE usage events including AI model invocations, token usage, and billing information.\n+\n+**Data Source**: Cursor API via Airbyte connector\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Schema Definition\n+\n+| Column | Type | Constraints | Description |\n+|--------|------|-------------|-------------|\n+| `unique` | text | PRIMARY KEY | Unique event identifier |\n+| `kind` | text | NOT NULL | Event type (e.g., \"chat\", \"completion\", \"agent\") |\n+| `model` | text | NOT NULL | AI model used (e.g., \"gpt-4\", \"claude-3.5-sonnet\") |\n+| `maxMode` | boolean | NOT NULL | Whether max mode was enabled |\n+| `timestamp` | timestamptz | NOT NULL | Event timestamp |\n+| `userEmail` | text | NOT NULL | User email address |","path":"streams/raw_cursor/cursor_events.md","commit_id":"7b4811e24e84830df73aabdea58e332784a65b32","original_commit_id":"9e1edb2dcc6d5ea476ba219a7577b99ed3772afd","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**PII stored with no data-governance note**\n\n`userEmail` contains personal data. The documentation has no mention of retention policy, access controls, anonymization, or compliance requirements (GDPR/CCPA). At a minimum, add a \"Data Privacy\" subsection under Notes flagging this as PII and pointing to the relevant policy.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@streams/raw_cursor/cursor_events.md` at line 20, Add a \"Data Privacy\"\nsubsection under the Notes section of streams/raw_cursor/cursor_events.md that\nexplicitly flags the `userEmail` field as PII; state the retention policy,\nrequired access controls, recommended anonymization/pseudonymization steps, and\nreference applicable compliance guidance (e.g., GDPR/CCPA) or an internal\ndata-governance policy link so consumers know handling and compliance\nrequirements for `userEmail`.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:triton:churro -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-02-23T09:54:25Z","updated_at":"2026-02-23T09:54:28Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/3#discussion_r2839934778","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/3","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/2839934778"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/3#discussion_r2839934778"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/3"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/2839934778/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":20,"original_line":20,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"NONE","original_position":20,"position":20,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/2839934782","pull_request_review_id":3840072782,"id":2839934782,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDORRWv8s6pRfc-","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,173 @@\n+# Table: `cursor_events`\n+\n+## Overview\n+\n+**Purpose**: Store individual Cursor IDE usage events including AI model invocations, token usage, and billing information.\n+\n+**Data Source**: Cursor API via Airbyte connector\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Schema Definition\n+\n+| Column | Type | Constraints | Description |\n+|--------|------|-------------|-------------|\n+| `unique` | text | PRIMARY KEY | Unique event identifier |\n+| `kind` | text | NOT NULL | Event type (e.g., \"chat\", \"completion\", \"agent\") |\n+| `model` | text | NOT NULL | AI model used (e.g., \"gpt-4\", \"claude-3.5-sonnet\") |\n+| `maxMode` | boolean | NOT NULL | Whether max mode was enabled |\n+| `timestamp` | timestamptz | NOT NULL | Event timestamp |\n+| `userEmail` | text | NOT NULL | User email address |\n+| `isHeadless` | boolean | NOT NULL | Whether event was headless (no UI) |\n+| `isChargeable` | boolean | NOT NULL | Whether event incurs charges |\n+| `requestsCosts` | numeric | NOT NULL | Request cost in credits |\n+| `cursorTokenFee` | numeric | NOT NULL | Cursor token fee |\n+| `isTokenBasedCall` | boolean | NOT NULL | Whether this is a token-based API call |\n+\n+**Indexes**:\n+- `idx_cursor_events_timestamp`: `(timestamp)`\n+- `idx_cursor_events_user_email`: `(userEmail)`\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Field Semantics\n+\n+### Core Identifiers\n+\n+**`unique`** (text, PRIMARY KEY)\n+- **Purpose**: Unique identifier for each event\n+- **Format**: Opaque string ID generated by Cursor\n+- **Usage**: Primary key, deduplication\n+\n+**`userEmail`** (text, NOT NULL)\n+- **Purpose**: Email of the user who triggered the event\n+- **Format**: Standard email format\n+- **Example**: \"developer@company.com\"\n+- **Usage**: User attribution, activity analysis\n+\n+### Event Classification\n+\n+**`kind`** (text, NOT NULL)\n+- **Purpose**: Type of AI interaction\n+- **Values**: \"chat\", \"completion\", \"agent\", \"cmd-k\", etc.\n+- **Usage**: Event categorization, feature usage analysis\n+\n+**`model`** (text, NOT NULL)\n+- **Purpose**: AI model used for the request\n+- **Examples**: \"gpt-4\", \"gpt-4o\", \"claude-3.5-sonnet\", \"cursor-small\"\n+- **Usage**: Model usage statistics, cost analysis\n+\n+**`maxMode`** (boolean, NOT NULL)\n+- **Purpose**: Whether the request used Cursor's max mode\n+- **Values**: true/false\n+- **Usage**: Feature adoption tracking\n+\n+**`isHeadless`** (boolean, NOT NULL)\n+- **Purpose**: Whether the event was triggered without UI interaction\n+- **Values**: true/false\n+- **Usage**: Automated vs interactive usage analysis\n+\n+### Billing\n+\n+**`isChargeable`** (boolean, NOT NULL)\n+- **Purpose**: Whether this event counts toward billing\n+- **Values**: true/false\n+- **Usage**: Cost tracking, billing analysis\n+\n+**`requestsCosts`** (numeric, NOT NULL)\n+- **Purpose**: Cost of the request in credits\n+- **Format**: Numeric value\n+- **Usage**: Cost analysis, budget monitoring\n+\n+**`cursorTokenFee`** (numeric, NOT NULL)\n+- **Purpose**: Cursor platform token fee\n+- **Format**: Numeric value\n+- **Usage**: Fee tracking\n+\n+**`isTokenBasedCall`** (boolean, NOT NULL)\n+- **Purpose**: Whether this call is billed by tokens rather than requests\n+- **Values**: true/false\n+- **Usage**: Billing model categorization\n+\n+### Timestamps\n+\n+**`timestamp`** (timestamptz, NOT NULL)\n+- **Purpose**: When the event occurred\n+- **Format**: ISO 8601 timestamp with timezone\n+- **Usage**: Time-series analysis, activity tracking\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Relationships\n+\n+### Children\n+\n+**`cursor_events_token_usage`**\n+- **Join**: `unique` → `event_unique`\n+- **Cardinality**: One event to one token usage record\n+- **Description**: Detailed token consumption for each event\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Usage Examples\n+\n+### Recent events by user\n+\n+```sql\n+SELECT\n+    \"unique\",\n+    kind,\n+    model,\n+    timestamp,\n+    requestsCosts\n+FROM cursor_events\n+WHERE userEmail = 'developer@company.com'\n+  AND timestamp > NOW() - INTERVAL '7 days'\n+ORDER BY timestamp DESC\n+LIMIT 100;\n+```\n+\n+### Model usage statistics\n+\n+```sql\n+SELECT\n+    model,\n+    kind,\n+    COUNT(*) as event_count,\n+    SUM(requestsCosts) as total_cost\n+FROM cursor_events\n+WHERE timestamp >= '2026-01-01'\n+GROUP BY model, kind\n+ORDER BY event_count DESC;\n+```\n+\n+### Daily usage per user\n+\n+```sql\n+SELECT\n+    userEmail,\n+    DATE(timestamp) as day,\n+    COUNT(*) as events,\n+    SUM(CASE WHEN isChargeable THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) as chargeable_events,\n+    SUM(requestsCosts) as total_cost\n+FROM cursor_events\n+WHERE timestamp >= NOW() - INTERVAL '30 days'\n+GROUP BY userEmail, DATE(timestamp)\n+ORDER BY day DESC, total_cost DESC;\n+```","path":"streams/raw_cursor/cursor_events.md","commit_id":"7b4811e24e84830df73aabdea58e332784a65b32","original_commit_id":"9e1edb2dcc6d5ea476ba219a7577b99ed3772afd","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Unquoted camelCase identifiers in SQL examples will silently break on PostgreSQL**\n\nBy default PostgreSQL folds all unquoted identifiers to lowercase, so `Username`, `USERNAME`, and `username` are all treated as the same identifier when written without quotes. Every camelCase column in the examples — `requestsCosts`, `userEmail`, `isChargeable` — is written unquoted, so PostgreSQL will look for `requestscosts`, `useremail`, `ischargeable`, etc. at query time. Either:\n\n1. The columns were created with unquoted names (stored lowercase), meaning the schema documentation is using incorrect casing throughout; **or**\n2. The columns were created quoted (preserving camelCase), meaning every SQL example needs double-quoting applied consistently.\n\nPick one canonical form and apply it across the schema table, field semantics, and all SQL examples.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@streams/raw_cursor/cursor_events.md` around lines 116 - 157, The SQL examples\nuse camelCase columns (requestsCosts, userEmail, isChargeable) that will be\nfolded to lowercase by PostgreSQL; update the examples to use a consistent\ncanonical form — either change all references to lowercase unquoted identifiers\n(requestscosts, useremail, ischargeable) and ensure the schema docs match, or\n(recommended) wrap every camelCase identifier in double quotes (e.g.,\n\"requestsCosts\", \"userEmail\", \"isChargeable\") throughout the SQL blocks and the\nschema table so the quoted names match the actual quoted column definitions on\ncursor_events and all documentation.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:triton:churro -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-02-23T09:54:25Z","updated_at":"2026-02-23T09:54:28Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/3#discussion_r2839934782","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/3","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/2839934782"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/3#discussion_r2839934782"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/3"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/2839934782/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":116,"original_start_line":116,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":157,"original_line":157,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"NONE","original_position":157,"position":157,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/2839934789","pull_request_review_id":3840072782,"id":2839934789,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDORRWv8s6pRfdF","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,126 @@\n+# Table: `git.author`\n+\n+## Overview\n+\n+**Purpose**: Store unique commit authors identified by normalized name and email combinations. Supports case-insensitive deduplication via generated columns.\n+\n+**Data Source**: Extracted from git commit metadata via GitLab API\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Schema Definition\n+\n+| Column | Type | Constraints | Description |\n+|--------|------|-------------|-------------|\n+| `id` | integer | PRIMARY KEY, AUTO INCREMENT | Auto-increment primary key |\n+| `name` | varchar(255) | NULLABLE | Original author name (preserves case) |\n+| `email` | varchar(255) | NULLABLE | Original author email (preserves case) |\n+| `name_lower` | varchar(255) | GENERATED | COALESCE(LOWER(name), '') |\n+| `email_lower` | varchar(255) | GENERATED | COALESCE(LOWER(email), '') |\n+| `created_at` | timestamp | DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP | Record creation timestamp |\n+\n+**Indexes**:\n+- `(name_lower, email_lower)` — UNIQUE, normalized author lookup","path":"streams/raw_git/git_author.md","commit_id":"7b4811e24e84830df73aabdea58e332784a65b32","original_commit_id":"9e1edb2dcc6d5ea476ba219a7577b99ed3772afd","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**NULL+NULL deduplication collapses all anonymous authors into a single row — ingestion will fail for the second occurrence.**\n\n`COALESCE(LOWER(name), '')` and `COALESCE(LOWER(email), '')` both produce `''` when the source field is NULL. Any commit with both `name=NULL` and `email=NULL` will map to `(name_lower='', email_lower='')`. Because of the UNIQUE constraint, only the **first** such commit's author can be inserted; every subsequent anonymous commit will raise a unique-constraint violation and fail ingestion.\n\nOptions:\n1. Use a surrogate deduplication key (e.g., a hash of `name_lower || '|' || email_lower` combined with a sequence for the all-null case) rather than relying solely on the generated columns for uniqueness.\n2. Use `NULL`-valued generated columns (no `COALESCE`) and rely on PostgreSQL's behavior that `NULL ≠ NULL` in unique indexes, while adding a separate index for lookups.\n\nThe Notes section should also explicitly document this single-slot limitation.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@streams/raw_git/git_author.md` around lines 18 - 23, Generated columns\nname_lower and email_lower currently use COALESCE(LOWER(...), '') which\ncollapses (NULL,NULL) into ('','') and breaks the UNIQUE index (name_lower,\nemail_lower); change the schema so anonymous authors don't collide by either 1)\nreplacing the COALESCE expressions with NULL-producing generated columns (e.g.,\nGENERATED AS (LOWER(name)) so NULL stays NULL) and keep the unique index\nbehavior that treats NULLs as distinct for multiple anonymous rows, or 2) add a\nsurrogate deduplication column (e.g., author_dedup_key) computed as a hash of\nLOWER(name)||'|'||LOWER(email) and handle the all-NULL case by appending a\nsequence or UUID to the hash, then enforce uniqueness on that surrogate instead\nof (name_lower,email_lower); also update the Notes to document the single-slot\nlimitation and which approach was chosen.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:triton:churro -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-02-23T09:54:25Z","updated_at":"2026-02-23T09:54:28Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/3#discussion_r2839934789","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/3","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/2839934789"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/3#discussion_r2839934789"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/3"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/2839934789/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":18,"original_start_line":18,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":23,"original_line":23,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"NONE","original_position":23,"position":23,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/2839934798","pull_request_review_id":3840072782,"id":2839934798,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDORRWv8s6pRfdO","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,167 @@\n+# Table: `git.loc`\n+\n+## Overview\n+\n+**Purpose**: Store daily lines-of-code (LOC) snapshots for files in tracked repositories, enabling LOC trend analysis over time.\n+\n+**Data Source**: Computed from repository file contents at default branch HEAD\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Schema Definition\n+\n+| Column | Type | Constraints | Description |\n+|--------|------|-------------|-------------|\n+| `id` | integer | PRIMARY KEY, AUTO INCREMENT | Internal primary key |\n+| `repo_id` | integer | NOT NULL | References repo.gitlab_repo_id |\n+| `file_id` | integer | NOT NULL | References file.id |\n+| `loc` | integer | NOT NULL | Lines of code count (0 for deleted/binary files) |\n+| `snapshot_date` | date | NOT NULL | UTC date for daily LOC snapshot |\n+| `commit_id` | integer | NOT NULL | Default branch HEAD commit at snapshot time |\n+| `created_at` | timestamp | NOT NULL, DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP | Snapshot timestamp |\n+\n+**Indexes**:\n+- `(repo_id, file_id, snapshot_date)` — UNIQUE, one LOC row per file per day\n+- `repo_id` — repository filtering\n+- `file_id` — file filtering\n+- `snapshot_date` — date-based queries\n+- `(repo_id, snapshot_date)` — daily snapshot queries by repo\n+- `created_at` — chronological ordering\n+- `(file_id, created_at)` — latest LOC per file queries\n+- `(repo_id, created_at)` — LOC history per repo\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Field Semantics\n+\n+### Core Identifiers\n+\n+**`id`** (integer, PRIMARY KEY)\n+- **Purpose**: Internal auto-increment key\n+\n+**`repo_id`** (integer, NOT NULL)\n+- **Purpose**: Reference to the parent repository\n+- **References**: `git.repo.gitlab_repo_id`\n+- **Usage**: Join key to repository\n+\n+**`file_id`** (integer, NOT NULL)\n+- **Purpose**: Reference to the file\n+- **References**: `git.file.id`\n+- **Usage**: Join key to file path\n+\n+**`commit_id`** (integer, NOT NULL)\n+- **Purpose**: The default branch HEAD commit at the time of snapshot\n+- **References**: `git.commit.id`\n+- **Usage**: Tracking which code version was measured\n+\n+### Metrics\n+\n+**`loc`** (integer, NOT NULL)\n+- **Purpose**: Lines of code in the file\n+- **Format**: Non-negative integer\n+- **Values**: 0 for deleted or binary files, positive for text files\n+- **Usage**: Codebase size tracking, growth analysis\n+\n+### Time\n+\n+**`snapshot_date`** (date, NOT NULL)\n+- **Purpose**: The date this LOC snapshot was taken\n+- **Format**: UTC date (YYYY-MM-DD)\n+- **Usage**: Time-series analysis, daily snapshots\n+\n+**`created_at`** (timestamp, NOT NULL)\n+- **Purpose**: Exact time the snapshot was created\n+- **Usage**: Ordering, freshness tracking\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Relationships\n+\n+### Parents\n+\n+**`git.repo`**\n+- **Join**: `repo_id` ← `gitlab_repo_id`\n+- **On Delete**: CASCADE\n+\n+**`git.file`**\n+- **Join**: `file_id` ← `id`\n+- **On Delete**: CASCADE\n+\n+**`git.commit`**\n+- **Join**: `commit_id` ← `id`\n+- **On Delete**: CASCADE","path":"streams/raw_git/git_loc.md","commit_id":"7b4811e24e84830df73aabdea58e332784a65b32","original_commit_id":"9e1edb2dcc6d5ea476ba219a7577b99ed3772afd","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**CASCADE from `git.commit` can silently destroy historical LOC data.**\n\nIf a commit is deleted (force-push, squash, or repo maintenance), every LOC snapshot that referenced it as the default-branch HEAD at capture time would be cascade-deleted. Snapshots are historical analytics records whose value is the `snapshot_date`, not the continued existence of the commit. Consider `ON DELETE RESTRICT` (or `SET NULL` if `commit_id` is made nullable) to protect the history while still enforcing referential integrity at write time.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@streams/raw_git/git_loc.md` around lines 90 - 92, The join from git.commit\n(column commit_id ← id) currently uses ON DELETE CASCADE which will delete\nhistorical LOC snapshots when commits are removed; change the foreign key\nconstraint on commit_id to use ON DELETE RESTRICT (or ON DELETE SET NULL if you\ndecide to make commit_id nullable) so snapshots aren’t cascade-deleted — update\nthe FK definition that references git.commit.id, adjust the commit_id column\nnullability if choosing SET NULL, and ensure any migration/schema change and\ntests reflect the new referential action.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:triton:churro -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-02-23T09:54:25Z","updated_at":"2026-02-23T09:54:28Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/3#discussion_r2839934798","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/3","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/2839934798"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/3#discussion_r2839934798"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/3"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/2839934798/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":90,"original_start_line":90,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":92,"original_line":92,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"NONE","original_position":92,"position":92,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/2839934805","pull_request_review_id":3840072782,"id":2839934805,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDORRWv8s6pRfdV","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,131 @@\n+# Table: `ms365_onedrive_activity`\n+\n+## Overview\n+\n+**Purpose**: Store Microsoft OneDrive activity reports per user, including file sync, view/edit, and sharing metrics.\n+\n+**Data Source**: Microsoft Graph API — OneDrive Activity Reports via Airbyte connector\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Schema Definition\n+\n+| Column | Type | Constraints | Description |\n+|--------|------|-------------|-------------|\n+| `unique` | text | PRIMARY KEY | Unique record identifier |","path":"streams/raw_ms365/ms365_onedrive_activity.md","commit_id":"7b4811e24e84830df73aabdea58e332784a65b32","original_commit_id":"9e1edb2dcc6d5ea476ba219a7577b99ed3772afd","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧩 Analysis chain</summary>\n\n🌐 Web query:\n\n`PostgreSQL reserved keywords UNIQUE`\n\n💡 Result:\n\nIn PostgreSQL, `UNIQUE` is a **reserved** SQL keyword, so you **can’t use it as an unquoted identifier** (e.g., table/column name). If you must use it, **double-quote** it (e.g., `\"unique\"`). [1]\n\n**Source:** PostgreSQL 18 docs, *Appendix C. SQL Key Words* (`UNIQUE` → “reserved”). [1]\n\n**References**\n[1] PostgreSQL Documentation (current/18): *Appendix C. SQL Key Words* ([postgresql.org](https://www.postgresql.org/docs/current/sql-keywords-appendix.html))\n\nCitations:\n\n- 1: https://www.postgresql.org/docs/current/sql-keywords-appendix.html\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# First, let's find and read the markdown file to see all table definitions\nfd \"ms365_onedrive_activity.md\" -t f\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/insight-spec\n\nLength of output: 112\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Also check if there are other related MS365 markdown files in the PR\nfd \"ms365.*\\.md\" -t f | head -20\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/insight-spec\n\nLength of output: 243\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\ncat -n streams/raw_ms365/ms365_onedrive_activity.md\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/insight-spec\n\nLength of output: 4926\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Check the other 3 files for the same `unique` column pattern\nfor file in streams/raw_ms365/ms365_email_activity.md streams/raw_ms365/ms365_sharepoint_activity.md streams/raw_ms365/ms365_teams_activity.md; do\n  echo \"=== $file ===\";\n  grep -n \"unique\" \"$file\" | head -5;\ndone\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/insight-spec\n\nLength of output: 781\n\n---\n\n\n\n</details>\n\n**Rename `unique` column — PostgreSQL reserved keyword will cause SQL errors**\n\n`unique` is a reserved PostgreSQL keyword and cannot be used as an unquoted column identifier in DDL or DML statements. Any `CREATE TABLE`, `SELECT`, `INSERT`, or `UPDATE` statement that references this column unquoted will fail.\n\nThis affects all four MS365 activity tables in this PR (ms365_onedrive_activity, ms365_email_activity, ms365_sharepoint_activity, ms365_teams_activity). Rename the column to a non-reserved identifier (e.g., `id`, `record_id`) across all schema definitions and corresponding SQL examples.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Example fix for ms365_onedrive_activity</summary>\n\n```diff\n-| `unique` | text | PRIMARY KEY | Unique record identifier |\n+| `id` | text | PRIMARY KEY | Unique record identifier |\n```\n\nUpdate Field Semantics section:\n\n```diff\n-**`unique`** (text, PRIMARY KEY)\n+**`id`** (text, PRIMARY KEY)\n - **Purpose**: Unique record identifier\n - **Usage**: Primary key, deduplication\n```\n\nApply the same changes to the other three schema files.\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Committable suggestion</summary>\n\n> ‼️ **IMPORTANT**\n> Carefully review the code before committing. Ensure that it accurately replaces the highlighted code, contains no missing lines, and has no issues with indentation. Thoroughly test & benchmark the code to ensure it meets the requirements.\n\n```suggestion\n| `id` | text | PRIMARY KEY | Unique record identifier |\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_end -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@streams/raw_ms365/ms365_onedrive_activity.md` at line 15, The schema uses a\ncolumn named `unique`, which is a PostgreSQL reserved keyword; rename that\ncolumn to a safe identifier (e.g., `id` or `record_id`) in every schema and\nexample SQL for all four tables (ms365_onedrive_activity, ms365_email_activity,\nms365_sharepoint_activity, ms365_teams_activity), update any PRIMARY KEY\nreferences and constraints that mention `unique`, and update the Field\nSemantics/description to reflect the new name so all CREATE TABLE, SELECT,\nINSERT, UPDATE examples and docs consistently use the new identifier.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:triton:churro -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-02-23T09:54:25Z","updated_at":"2026-02-23T09:54:28Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/3#discussion_r2839934805","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/3","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/2839934805"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/3#discussion_r2839934805"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/3"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/2839934805/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":15,"original_line":15,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"NONE","original_position":15,"position":15,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/2839934818","pull_request_review_id":3840072782,"id":2839934818,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDORRWv8s6pRfdi","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,121 @@\n+# Table: `zulip_messages`\n+\n+## Overview\n+\n+**Purpose**: Store aggregated Zulip message counts per user per time period, tracking messaging activity over time.\n+\n+**Data Source**: Zulip API via Airbyte connector\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Schema Definition\n+\n+| Column | Type | Constraints | Description |\n+|--------|------|-------------|-------------|\n+| `uniq` | text | PRIMARY KEY | Unique record identifier |","path":"streams/raw_zulip/zulip_messages.md","commit_id":"7b4811e24e84830df73aabdea58e332784a65b32","original_commit_id":"9e1edb2dcc6d5ea476ba219a7577b99ed3772afd","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_🛠️ Refactor suggestion_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**`uniq` primary key: opaque name with undocumented composition**\n\nThe name `uniq` conveys no information about what the key represents. Neither the Schema Definition nor the Field Semantics section explains how this value is derived (e.g., a hash of `sender_id || created_at`, a UUID, a composite string). Without this, consumers cannot understand deduplication logic or reproduce the key.\n\nRename to something descriptive (e.g., `message_agg_id` or `agg_key`) and add a **Format** / **Derivation** entry to the Field Semantics section.\n\n\n\n\nAlso applies to: 30-32\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@streams/raw_zulip/zulip_messages.md` at line 15, Rename the opaque `uniq`\nprimary key to a descriptive name (e.g., `message_agg_id` or `agg_key`) in the\nschema table and any other occurrences (also update the instances noted around\nlines 30-32), and add a Format/Derivation entry in the Field Semantics section\nthat clearly describes how the value is generated (for example: \"Format:\nhex-encoded SHA256(sender_id || '|' || created_at || '|' || message_id)\" or\n\"UUID v4\"; include exact concatenation/order and hashing algorithm or note that\nit is a UUID) so consumers can reproduce deduplication logic and validate keys.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:triton:churro -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-02-23T09:54:25Z","updated_at":"2026-02-23T09:54:28Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/3#discussion_r2839934818","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/3","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/2839934818"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/3#discussion_r2839934818"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/3"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/2839934818/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":15,"original_line":15,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"NONE","original_position":15,"position":15,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/2839934825","pull_request_review_id":3840072782,"id":2839934825,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDORRWv8s6pRfdp","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,396 @@\n+# Table: `communication_events`\n+\n+## Overview\n+\n+**Purpose**: Unified audit log of communication activities across all platforms. Normalizes messaging, email, meeting, and call events from multiple sources into a single stream for cross-platform communication analysis.\n+\n+**Data Sources**:\n+- `raw_ms365/ms365_teams_activity` — Teams chats, channel posts, calls, meetings\n+- `raw_ms365/ms365_email_activity` — Email send/receive/read\n+- `raw_zulip/zulip_messages` — Zulip chat messages\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Schema Definition\n+\n+| Column | Type | Constraints | Description |\n+|--------|------|-------------|-------------|\n+| `id` | bigint | PRIMARY KEY, AUTO INCREMENT | Internal primary key |\n+| `ingestion_date` | timestamp | NOT NULL | When this record was ingested into the stream |\n+| `source_id` | text | NOT NULL | Unique identifier of the source record |\n+| `event_date` | date | NOT NULL | Date of the communication event |\n+| `source` | text | NOT NULL | Source platform identifier |\n+| `user_email` | text | NOT NULL | User email (unified identifier) |\n+| `user_display_name` | text | NULLABLE | User display name from source |\n+| `channel` | text | NOT NULL | Communication channel type |\n+| `direction` | text | NULLABLE | Communication direction |\n+| `count` | numeric | NOT NULL | Number of events/messages |\n+| `metadata` | jsonb | NULLABLE | Source-specific additional data |\n+\n+**Indexes**:\n+- `idx_comm_events_ingestion`: `(ingestion_date)` — incremental sync\n+- `idx_comm_events_source_id`: `(source_id)` — source record lookup\n+- `idx_comm_events_date`: `(event_date)`\n+- `idx_comm_events_user`: `(user_email)`\n+- `idx_comm_events_source`: `(source)`\n+- `idx_comm_events_channel`: `(channel)`\n+- `(user_email, event_date)` — user activity over time\n+- `(source, channel, event_date)` — source/channel trends\n+- `(source, source_id)` — UNIQUE, prevents duplicate ingestion from same source record\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Field Semantics\n+\n+### Core Identifiers\n+\n+**`id`** (bigint, PRIMARY KEY)\n+- **Purpose**: Auto-increment primary key\n+- **Usage**: Unique record identification\n+\n+**`ingestion_date`** (timestamp, NOT NULL)\n+- **Purpose**: Timestamp of when this record was ingested into the communication stream\n+- **Format**: PostgreSQL timestamp (e.g., \"2026-02-23 14:30:00\")\n+- **Usage**: Incremental synchronization — downstream consumers query `WHERE ingestion_date > last_sync_timestamp` to pick up only new records since last run\n+- **Note**: This is NOT the event date. A record may be ingested days after the event occurred (e.g., when backfilling historical data or when a source report becomes available with delay)\n+\n+**`source_id`** (text, NOT NULL)\n+- **Purpose**: Unique identifier of the original record in the source system, enabling traceability back to the raw data\n+- **Format**: Composite key as `{source}:{unique_id}:{channel}` to ensure uniqueness across sources and channels\n+- **Derived from**:\n+  - MS365 Teams: `ms365_teams:{unique}:{channel}` (e.g., `ms365_teams:abc123:chat_group`)\n+  - MS365 Email: `ms365_email:{unique}:{channel}` (e.g., `ms365_email:def456:email_sent`)\n+  - Zulip: `zulip:{uniq}` (e.g., `zulip:msg_789`)\n+- **Usage**: Trace back to source record, deduplication, reprocessing detection\n+- **Note**: Combined with `source`, forms a unique constraint to prevent duplicate ingestion\n+\n+**`event_date`** (date, NOT NULL)\n+- **Purpose**: Date when the communication occurred\n+- **Format**: YYYY-MM-DD\n+- **Derived from**:\n+  - MS365: `reportRefreshDate`\n+  - Zulip: `DATE(created_at)`\n+- **Usage**: Time-series analysis, daily aggregations","path":"streams/stream_communication/communication_events.md","commit_id":"7b4811e24e84830df73aabdea58e332784a65b32","original_commit_id":"9e1edb2dcc6d5ea476ba219a7577b99ed3772afd","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧩 Analysis chain</summary>\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\nrg -n \"reportDate|reportRefreshDate\" --type=md\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/insight-spec\n\nLength of output: 3704\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Get the full context of the file mentioned in the review\ncat -n streams/stream_communication/communication_events.md | head -200\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/insight-spec\n\nLength of output: 9412\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Check if there are any MS365-related configuration or schema files\nfd -type f -name \"*.md\" -o -name \"*.yml\" -o -name \"*.yaml\" -o -name \"*.json\" | head -20\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/insight-spec\n\nLength of output: 238\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\nsed -n '150,210p' streams/stream_communication/communication_events.md\n```\n\nRepository: cyberfabric/insight-spec\n\nLength of output: 1991\n\n---\n\n\n\n</details>\n\n**Clarify `event_date` semantics for MS365 period-based data.**\n\nThe `event_date` field's documented **Purpose** (\"Date when the communication occurred\") conflicts with its actual derivation for MS365 sources. Since MS365 reports are period-based (typically 7 days), each row represents cumulative activity across that window, and `reportRefreshDate` is Microsoft's data-freshness timestamp — not the date activity occurred. This can lag by days or more.\n\nAssigning one `reportRefreshDate` to a week's worth of activity collapses fine-grained time-series analysis. A Teams message from Monday and emails received Friday both receive the same `event_date`, making cross-platform comparison with Zulip (which has daily granularity via `created_at`) fundamentally misleading.\n\nNo `reportDate` field exists in the raw MS365 tables to use instead.\n\n**Update the field semantics to clarify:**\n- Revise `event_date` Purpose for MS365 data: \"For MS365, represents the report refresh date (end of the reporting period), not the individual activity date. Multiple activity types across a 7-day window map to a single date.\"\n- Document the implication: time-series analysis and cross-platform day-level correlation are not reliable for MS365 sources due to period-based aggregation.\n- Consider storing the raw `reportRefreshDate` in `metadata` to preserve the distinction for downstream consumers aware of the limitation.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@streams/stream_communication/communication_events.md` around lines 67 - 73,\nUpdate the documentation for the event_date field to clarify MS365 semantics:\nchange the Purpose text for event_date when sourced from MS365 to state it\nrepresents the report refresh date (end of the reporting period) rather than the\nactual activity date, note that MS365 rows are period-aggregated (typically 7\ndays) so day-level time-series and cross-platform comparisons with Zulip's\nDATE(created_at) are unreliable, and add a recommendation to preserve the\noriginal reportRefreshDate in metadata so downstream consumers can distinguish\nperiod-end timestamps from per-event dates.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:triton:churro -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-02-23T09:54:25Z","updated_at":"2026-02-23T09:54:28Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/3#discussion_r2839934825","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/3","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/2839934825"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/3#discussion_r2839934825"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/3"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/2839934825/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":67,"original_start_line":67,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":73,"original_line":73,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"NONE","original_position":73,"position":73,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/2839934838","pull_request_review_id":3840072782,"id":2839934838,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDORRWv8s6pRfd2","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,214 @@\n+# Table: `class_task_tracker`\n+\n+## Overview\n+\n+**Purpose**: Store unified task/issue data from multiple task tracker sources (YouTrack, Jira) with lifecycle timestamps and ownership information.\n+\n+**Data Sources**:\n+- YouTrack: `source = \"youtrack\"`\n+- Jira: `source = \"jira\"`\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Schema Definition\n+\n+| Column | Type | Constraints | Description |\n+|--------|------|-------------|-------------|\n+| `id` | int | PRIMARY KEY, AUTO INCREMENT | Internal primary key |\n+| `ingestion_at` | timestamp | NOT NULL | Ingestion date |\n+| `deleted` | boolean | NOT NULL | Record deletion flag |\n+| `task_id` | text | NOT NULL | Human-readable task identifier |\n+| `task_id_ref` | text | NOT NULL | Task identifier in source tracker system |\n+| `source` | text | NOT NULL | Source marker: \"youtrack\" or \"jira\" |\n+| `metadata` | jsonb | NOT NULL | Free-form metadata |\n+| `created_at` | timestamp | NOT NULL | Task creation datetime |\n+| `created_by_name` | text | NOT NULL | Task creator name |\n+| `created_by_id` | text | NOT NULL | Task creator identifier in tracker |\n+| `started_at` | timestamp | NULLABLE | Task start datetime |\n+| `started_by_name` | text | NULLABLE | Task starter name |\n+| `started_by_id` | text | NULLABLE | Task starter identifier in tracker |\n+| `testing_started_at` | timestamp | NULLABLE | Testing start datetime |\n+| `testing_started_by_name` | text | NULLABLE | Testing starter name |\n+| `testing_started_by_id` | text | NULLABLE | Testing starter identifier in tracker |\n+| `done_at` | timestamp | NULLABLE | Task completion datetime |\n+| `done_by_name` | text | NULLABLE | Task completer name |\n+| `done_by_id` | text | NULLABLE | Task completer identifier in tracker |\n+\n+**Indexes**:\n+- `idx_class_task_tracker_ingestion_at`: `(ingestion_at)`\n+- `idx_class_task_tracker_task_id`: `(task_id)`\n+- `idx_class_task_tracker_task_id_ref`: `(task_id_ref)`\n+- `idx_class_task_tracker_source_task_id_ref`: `(source, task_id_ref)`\n+- `uq_class_task_tracker_source_task_id_ref_deleted`: `(source, task_id_ref, deleted)` — UNIQUE\n+","path":"streams/stream_task_tracker/task_tracker.md","commit_id":"b079580cc3ce130cb78f98ecae10f237fb10b604","original_commit_id":"9e1edb2dcc6d5ea476ba219a7577b99ed3772afd","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**The unique constraint on `(source, task_id_ref, deleted)` does not prevent duplicate active tasks — and the Notes section is misleading.**\n\nIncluding `deleted` in the key means `(source, task_id_ref, false)` and `(source, task_id_ref, true)` are treated as **distinct** rows and can coexist simultaneously. Any query that omits `AND deleted = false` will return two rows for the same logical task. The Notes section says this \"ensures no duplicate tasks per source,\" which is incorrect — it only prevents two active records or two deleted records from existing, not both at the same time.\n\nFor true uniqueness of the live record, the constraint should be `(source, task_id_ref)`. Re-ingestion of a previously deleted task would then require an `UPDATE` (flip `deleted` back to `false`) rather than a new `INSERT`.\n\nIf the intent is specifically to retain both the deleted and the active record for audit purposes, that decision should be explicitly called out in the Notes, and consumers need a strong reminder to always filter `deleted = false`.\n\n<details>\n<summary>✏️ Proposed fix (if one canonical row per task is the intent)</summary>\n\n```diff\n-| `uq_class_task_tracker_source_task_id_ref_deleted`: `(source, task_id_ref, deleted)` — UNIQUE\n+| `uq_class_task_tracker_source_task_id_ref`: `(source, task_id_ref)` — UNIQUE\n```\n\nAnd in Notes:\n```diff\n-The unique constraint on `(source, task_id_ref, deleted)` ensures no duplicate tasks per source.\n+The unique constraint on `(source, task_id_ref)` ensures at most one row (active or deleted) per task per source.\n```\n</details>\n\n\n\n\nAlso applies to: 202-202\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@streams/stream_task_tracker/task_tracker.md` around lines 42 - 43, The UNIQUE\nconstraint uq_class_task_tracker_source_task_id_ref_deleted currently includes\ndeleted, so (source, task_id_ref, false) and (source, task_id_ref, true) can\ncoexist and the Notes claim is inaccurate; change the constraint to enforce\nuniqueness on (source, task_id_ref) instead of (source, task_id_ref, deleted) so\nonly one canonical row per task exists (re-ingestion must UPDATE to set\ndeleted=false), and update the Notes to remove the misleading statement and\ndocument the new behavior; alternatively, if keeping both deleted/active rows is\nintentional, clarify that in Notes and add a strong reminder that all consumers\nmust include AND deleted = false in queries.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:triton:churro -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-02-23T09:54:25Z","updated_at":"2026-02-23T09:54:28Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/3#discussion_r2839934838","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/3","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/2839934838"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/3#discussion_r2839934838"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/3"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/2839934838/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":42,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":43,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"NONE","original_position":43,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/2840140379","pull_request_review_id":3840288777,"id":2840140379,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDORRWv8s6pSRpb","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,339 @@\n+# Table: `task`\n+\n+## Overview\n+\n+**Purpose**: Store individual task/sub-task work items with lifecycle timestamps and authorship. Tasks represent the smallest actionable units of work, typically implementing part of a user story.\n+\n+**Data Sources**:\n+- YouTrack: `source = \"youtrack\"`\n+- Jira: `source = \"jira\"`\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Schema Definition\n+\n+| Column | Type | Constraints | Description |\n+|--------|------|-------------|-------------|\n+| `id` | bigint | PRIMARY KEY, AUTO INCREMENT | Internal primary key |\n+| `ingestion_date` | timestamp | NOT NULL | When this record was ingested |\n+| `source` | text | NOT NULL | Source tracker: \"youtrack\" or \"jira\" |\n+| `source_id` | text | NOT NULL | Identifier in source tracker system |\n+| `task_id` | text | NOT NULL | Human-readable task ID (e.g., \"MON-305\") |\n+| `user_story_id` | text | NULLABLE | Parent user story ID (e.g., \"MON-201\") |","path":"streams/stream_task_tracker/task.md","commit_id":"b079580cc3ce130cb78f98ecae10f237fb10b604","original_commit_id":"b079580cc3ce130cb78f98ecae10f237fb10b604","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**`user_story_id` join is missing a `source` filter — cross-source ID collision risk.**\n\n`user_story_id` stores a human-readable text ID (e.g., `\"MON-201\"`). The documented join is `task.user_story_id = user_story.task_id` without a `source` predicate. Since the schema explicitly supports two source systems (YouTrack and Jira), both can theoretically produce the same ID string. Every hierarchy query and rollup metric will silently cross-join rows from different source systems.\n\nThe relationship description (Line 185) and note (Line 335) should document the required `source` guard:\n\n```diff\n-**Join**: `user_story_id` ← `task_id`\n+**Join**: `task.user_story_id = user_story.task_id AND task.source = user_story.source`\n```\n\nAnd example queries involving this join should include:\n\n```sql\nJOIN user_story us\n  ON t.user_story_id = us.task_id\n AND t.source = us.source\n```\n\n\n\n\nAlso applies to: 185-185, 335-335\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@streams/stream_task_tracker/task.md` at line 22, The join using\ntask.user_story_id = user_story.task_id must include a source guard to avoid\ncross-source collisions: update the relationship description that references\nuser_story_id and any examples (including the note) to require AND t.source =\nus.source (or equivalent aliases) when joining task -> user_story; update all\nexample queries and the relationship/note text to show the safe pattern (e.g.,\nJOIN user_story us ON t.user_story_id = us.task_id AND t.source = us.source) and\nmention that source must match because IDs are not globally unique across\nYouTrack and Jira.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:triton:churro -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-02-23T10:41:20Z","updated_at":"2026-02-23T10:41:21Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/3#discussion_r2840140379","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/3","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/2840140379"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/3#discussion_r2840140379"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/3"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/2840140379/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":22,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"NONE","original_position":22,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/2840140385","pull_request_review_id":3840288777,"id":2840140385,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDORRWv8s6pSRph","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,339 @@\n+# Table: `task`\n+\n+## Overview\n+\n+**Purpose**: Store individual task/sub-task work items with lifecycle timestamps and authorship. Tasks represent the smallest actionable units of work, typically implementing part of a user story.\n+\n+**Data Sources**:\n+- YouTrack: `source = \"youtrack\"`\n+- Jira: `source = \"jira\"`\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Schema Definition\n+\n+| Column | Type | Constraints | Description |\n+|--------|------|-------------|-------------|\n+| `id` | bigint | PRIMARY KEY, AUTO INCREMENT | Internal primary key |\n+| `ingestion_date` | timestamp | NOT NULL | When this record was ingested |\n+| `source` | text | NOT NULL | Source tracker: \"youtrack\" or \"jira\" |\n+| `source_id` | text | NOT NULL | Identifier in source tracker system |\n+| `task_id` | text | NOT NULL | Human-readable task ID (e.g., \"MON-305\") |\n+| `user_story_id` | text | NULLABLE | Parent user story ID (e.g., \"MON-201\") |\n+| `deleted` | boolean | NOT NULL, DEFAULT false | Soft delete flag |\n+| `summary` | text | NOT NULL | Task title/summary |\n+| `project` | text | NULLABLE | Project key |\n+| `priority` | text | NULLABLE | Priority level |\n+| `estimation` | numeric | NULLABLE | Time estimation (hours) |\n+| `sprint` | text | NULLABLE | Current sprint name |\n+| `assignee_name` | text | NULLABLE | Current assignee name |\n+| `assignee_id` | text | NULLABLE | Current assignee ID in tracker |\n+| `labels` | text[] | NULLABLE | Labels/tags |\n+| `created_at` | timestamp | NOT NULL | Task creation datetime |\n+| `created_by_name` | text | NOT NULL | Creator name |\n+| `created_by_id` | text | NOT NULL | Creator ID in tracker |\n+| `started_at` | timestamp | NULLABLE | When work on the task began |\n+| `started_by_name` | text | NULLABLE | Who started the task |\n+| `started_by_id` | text | NULLABLE | Starter ID in tracker |\n+| `to_verify_at` | timestamp | NULLABLE | When task was moved to verification |\n+| `to_verify_by_name` | text | NULLABLE | Who moved it to verification |\n+| `to_verify_by_id` | text | NULLABLE | Verifier-mover ID in tracker |\n+| `done_at` | timestamp | NULLABLE | Task completion datetime |\n+| `done_by_name` | text | NULLABLE | Who completed the task |\n+| `done_by_id` | text | NULLABLE | Completer ID in tracker |\n+| `metadata` | jsonb | NULLABLE | Source-specific additional data |\n+\n+**Indexes**:\n+- `idx_task_ingestion_date`: `(ingestion_date)` — incremental sync\n+- `idx_task_task_id`: `(task_id)`\n+- `idx_task_user_story_id`: `(user_story_id)` — parent story lookup\n+- `idx_task_project`: `(project)`\n+- `idx_task_sprint`: `(sprint)`\n+- `idx_task_assignee_id`: `(assignee_id)` — workload queries\n+- `idx_task_created_at`: `(created_at)`\n+- `idx_task_done_at`: `(done_at)`\n+- `(source, source_id)` — UNIQUE, prevents duplicates\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Field Semantics\n+\n+### Core Identifiers\n+\n+**`id`** (bigint, PRIMARY KEY)\n+- **Purpose**: Internal auto-increment key\n+\n+**`source`** (text, NOT NULL)\n+- **Purpose**: Identifies the source tracker system\n+- **Values**: \"youtrack\", \"jira\"\n+\n+**`source_id`** (text, NOT NULL)\n+- **Purpose**: Identifier in the source tracker system\n+- **Usage**: Trace back to source, deduplication\n+\n+**`task_id`** (text, NOT NULL)\n+- **Purpose**: Human-readable task identifier\n+- **Format**: \"PROJECT-NUMBER\" (e.g., \"MON-305\")\n+- **Usage**: Display, cross-referencing with commit messages\n+\n+**`user_story_id`** (text, NULLABLE)\n+- **Purpose**: Human-readable ID of the parent user story\n+- **Format**: \"PROJECT-NUMBER\" (e.g., \"MON-201\")\n+- **Note**: NULL if task is standalone (not linked to a story)\n+- **Usage**: Story→task hierarchy, rollup metrics\n+\n+### Task Details\n+\n+**`summary`** (text, NOT NULL)\n+- **Purpose**: Task title/summary\n+- **Examples**: \"Fix login timeout bug\", \"Add email validation\"\n+\n+**`project`** (text, NULLABLE)\n+- **Purpose**: Project key\n+- **Examples**: \"MON\", \"PLAT\"\n+\n+**`priority`** (text, NULLABLE)\n+- **Purpose**: Priority level\n+- **Examples**: \"Critical\", \"Major\", \"Normal\", \"Minor\"\n+\n+**`estimation`** (numeric, NULLABLE)\n+- **Purpose**: Estimated effort in hours\n+- **Examples**: 2, 4, 8, 16\n+- **Usage**: Estimation accuracy analysis, capacity planning\n+\n+**`sprint`** (text, NULLABLE)\n+- **Purpose**: Current or last sprint\n+- **Examples**: \"Sprint 24.1\", \"2026-W08\"\n+\n+**`assignee_name`** / **`assignee_id`** (text, NULLABLE)\n+- **Purpose**: Current assignee\n+- **Usage**: Workload analysis, developer metrics\n+\n+**`labels`** (text[], NULLABLE)\n+- **Purpose**: Labels/tags\n+\n+### Lifecycle — Creation\n+\n+**`created_at`** (timestamp, NOT NULL)\n+- **Purpose**: When the task was created\n+\n+**`created_by_name`** (text, NOT NULL)\n+- **Purpose**: Creator name\n+\n+**`created_by_id`** (text, NOT NULL)\n+- **Purpose**: Creator ID in tracker\n+\n+### Lifecycle — Started (In Progress)\n+\n+**`started_at`** (timestamp, NULLABLE)\n+- **Purpose**: When work on the task began (moved to \"In Progress\")\n+- **Note**: NULL if task hasn't been started\n+- **Usage**: Lead time (created → started), reaction time\n+\n+**`started_by_name`** (text, NULLABLE)\n+- **Purpose**: Who started working on the task\n+\n+**`started_by_id`** (text, NULLABLE)\n+- **Purpose**: Starter ID in tracker\n+\n+### Lifecycle — To Verify\n+\n+**`to_verify_at`** (timestamp, NULLABLE)\n+- **Purpose**: When the task was moved to verification/review state\n+- **Note**: NULL if task hasn't reached verification\n+- **Usage**: Development time (started → to_verify), review queue time\n+\n+**`to_verify_by_name`** (text, NULLABLE)\n+- **Purpose**: Who moved the task to verification\n+\n+**`to_verify_by_id`** (text, NULLABLE)\n+- **Purpose**: ID in tracker of the person who moved it to verification\n+\n+### Lifecycle — Done\n+\n+**`done_at`** (timestamp, NULLABLE)\n+- **Purpose**: When the task was completed\n+- **Note**: NULL if task is not done\n+- **Usage**: Verification time (to_verify → done), total cycle time (started → done)\n+\n+**`done_by_name`** (text, NULLABLE)\n+- **Purpose**: Who completed/verified the task\n+\n+**`done_by_id`** (text, NULLABLE)\n+- **Purpose**: Completer ID in tracker\n+\n+### System Fields\n+\n+**`ingestion_date`** (timestamp, NOT NULL)\n+- **Purpose**: When the record was ingested\n+- **Usage**: Incremental sync\n+\n+**`deleted`** (boolean, NOT NULL, DEFAULT false)\n+- **Purpose**: Soft delete flag\n+\n+**`metadata`** (jsonb, NULLABLE)\n+- **Purpose**: Source-specific fields\n+- **Examples**: `{\"resolution\": \"Fixed\", \"branch\": \"feature/MON-305\", \"spent_time\": \"4h\"}`\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Relationships\n+\n+### Parent\n+\n+**`user_story`**\n+- **Join**: `user_story_id` ← `task_id`\n+- **Cardinality**: Many tasks to one user story\n+- **Description**: Parent story this task implements\n+\n+### Cross-Stream\n+\n+- **Git commits**: `task_id` matches `raw_git.git_commit.task_id` — directly links tasks to code changes\n+- **Communication**: Correlate task activity with `stream_communication` events via assignee email","path":"streams/stream_task_tracker/task.md","commit_id":"b079580cc3ce130cb78f98ecae10f237fb10b604","original_commit_id":"b079580cc3ce130cb78f98ecae10f237fb10b604","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Cross-stream communication correlation references \"email\" but the schema has no email field.**\n\nThe schema only carries `assignee_id` and `assignee_name`; there is no `assignee_email` column. If `stream_communication` links users by email, the join cannot be made directly. The documentation should either:\n- Add an `assignee_email` column to the schema, or\n- Clarify that `assignee_id` is expected to be the user's email in specific trackers (e.g., Jira), or\n- Reference an intermediate identity-resolution mapping table.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@streams/stream_task_tracker/task.md` at line 192, The doc line stating\n\"Correlate task activity with `stream_communication` events via assignee email\"\nis inconsistent with the schema (which only has `assignee_id` and\n`assignee_name`); update the documentation for `stream_task_tracker` to either\nadd an `assignee_email` column to the schema, or explicitly state that\n`assignee_id` will contain the user's email for trackers that support it (e.g.,\nJira), or point to the identity-resolution mapping table that joins\n`assignee_id` to emails so consumers know how to perform the correlation with\n`stream_communication`; reference `assignee_id`, `assignee_name`, and\n`stream_communication` in the change so it's clear where to apply the fix.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:triton:churro -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-02-23T10:41:20Z","updated_at":"2026-02-23T10:41:21Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/3#discussion_r2840140385","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/3","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/2840140385"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/3#discussion_r2840140385"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/3"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/2840140385/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":192,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"NONE","original_position":192,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/2840140390","pull_request_review_id":3840288777,"id":2840140390,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDORRWv8s6pSRpm","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,339 @@\n+# Table: `task`\n+\n+## Overview\n+\n+**Purpose**: Store individual task/sub-task work items with lifecycle timestamps and authorship. Tasks represent the smallest actionable units of work, typically implementing part of a user story.\n+\n+**Data Sources**:\n+- YouTrack: `source = \"youtrack\"`\n+- Jira: `source = \"jira\"`\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Schema Definition\n+\n+| Column | Type | Constraints | Description |\n+|--------|------|-------------|-------------|\n+| `id` | bigint | PRIMARY KEY, AUTO INCREMENT | Internal primary key |\n+| `ingestion_date` | timestamp | NOT NULL | When this record was ingested |\n+| `source` | text | NOT NULL | Source tracker: \"youtrack\" or \"jira\" |\n+| `source_id` | text | NOT NULL | Identifier in source tracker system |\n+| `task_id` | text | NOT NULL | Human-readable task ID (e.g., \"MON-305\") |\n+| `user_story_id` | text | NULLABLE | Parent user story ID (e.g., \"MON-201\") |\n+| `deleted` | boolean | NOT NULL, DEFAULT false | Soft delete flag |\n+| `summary` | text | NOT NULL | Task title/summary |\n+| `project` | text | NULLABLE | Project key |\n+| `priority` | text | NULLABLE | Priority level |\n+| `estimation` | numeric | NULLABLE | Time estimation (hours) |\n+| `sprint` | text | NULLABLE | Current sprint name |\n+| `assignee_name` | text | NULLABLE | Current assignee name |\n+| `assignee_id` | text | NULLABLE | Current assignee ID in tracker |\n+| `labels` | text[] | NULLABLE | Labels/tags |\n+| `created_at` | timestamp | NOT NULL | Task creation datetime |\n+| `created_by_name` | text | NOT NULL | Creator name |\n+| `created_by_id` | text | NOT NULL | Creator ID in tracker |\n+| `started_at` | timestamp | NULLABLE | When work on the task began |\n+| `started_by_name` | text | NULLABLE | Who started the task |\n+| `started_by_id` | text | NULLABLE | Starter ID in tracker |\n+| `to_verify_at` | timestamp | NULLABLE | When task was moved to verification |\n+| `to_verify_by_name` | text | NULLABLE | Who moved it to verification |\n+| `to_verify_by_id` | text | NULLABLE | Verifier-mover ID in tracker |\n+| `done_at` | timestamp | NULLABLE | Task completion datetime |\n+| `done_by_name` | text | NULLABLE | Who completed the task |\n+| `done_by_id` | text | NULLABLE | Completer ID in tracker |\n+| `metadata` | jsonb | NULLABLE | Source-specific additional data |\n+\n+**Indexes**:\n+- `idx_task_ingestion_date`: `(ingestion_date)` — incremental sync\n+- `idx_task_task_id`: `(task_id)`\n+- `idx_task_user_story_id`: `(user_story_id)` — parent story lookup\n+- `idx_task_project`: `(project)`\n+- `idx_task_sprint`: `(sprint)`\n+- `idx_task_assignee_id`: `(assignee_id)` — workload queries\n+- `idx_task_created_at`: `(created_at)`\n+- `idx_task_done_at`: `(done_at)`\n+- `(source, source_id)` — UNIQUE, prevents duplicates\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Field Semantics\n+\n+### Core Identifiers\n+\n+**`id`** (bigint, PRIMARY KEY)\n+- **Purpose**: Internal auto-increment key\n+\n+**`source`** (text, NOT NULL)\n+- **Purpose**: Identifies the source tracker system\n+- **Values**: \"youtrack\", \"jira\"\n+\n+**`source_id`** (text, NOT NULL)\n+- **Purpose**: Identifier in the source tracker system\n+- **Usage**: Trace back to source, deduplication\n+\n+**`task_id`** (text, NOT NULL)\n+- **Purpose**: Human-readable task identifier\n+- **Format**: \"PROJECT-NUMBER\" (e.g., \"MON-305\")\n+- **Usage**: Display, cross-referencing with commit messages\n+\n+**`user_story_id`** (text, NULLABLE)\n+- **Purpose**: Human-readable ID of the parent user story\n+- **Format**: \"PROJECT-NUMBER\" (e.g., \"MON-201\")\n+- **Note**: NULL if task is standalone (not linked to a story)\n+- **Usage**: Story→task hierarchy, rollup metrics\n+\n+### Task Details\n+\n+**`summary`** (text, NOT NULL)\n+- **Purpose**: Task title/summary\n+- **Examples**: \"Fix login timeout bug\", \"Add email validation\"\n+\n+**`project`** (text, NULLABLE)\n+- **Purpose**: Project key\n+- **Examples**: \"MON\", \"PLAT\"\n+\n+**`priority`** (text, NULLABLE)\n+- **Purpose**: Priority level\n+- **Examples**: \"Critical\", \"Major\", \"Normal\", \"Minor\"\n+\n+**`estimation`** (numeric, NULLABLE)\n+- **Purpose**: Estimated effort in hours\n+- **Examples**: 2, 4, 8, 16\n+- **Usage**: Estimation accuracy analysis, capacity planning\n+\n+**`sprint`** (text, NULLABLE)\n+- **Purpose**: Current or last sprint\n+- **Examples**: \"Sprint 24.1\", \"2026-W08\"\n+\n+**`assignee_name`** / **`assignee_id`** (text, NULLABLE)\n+- **Purpose**: Current assignee\n+- **Usage**: Workload analysis, developer metrics\n+\n+**`labels`** (text[], NULLABLE)\n+- **Purpose**: Labels/tags\n+\n+### Lifecycle — Creation\n+\n+**`created_at`** (timestamp, NOT NULL)\n+- **Purpose**: When the task was created\n+\n+**`created_by_name`** (text, NOT NULL)\n+- **Purpose**: Creator name\n+\n+**`created_by_id`** (text, NOT NULL)\n+- **Purpose**: Creator ID in tracker\n+\n+### Lifecycle — Started (In Progress)\n+\n+**`started_at`** (timestamp, NULLABLE)\n+- **Purpose**: When work on the task began (moved to \"In Progress\")\n+- **Note**: NULL if task hasn't been started\n+- **Usage**: Lead time (created → started), reaction time\n+\n+**`started_by_name`** (text, NULLABLE)\n+- **Purpose**: Who started working on the task\n+\n+**`started_by_id`** (text, NULLABLE)\n+- **Purpose**: Starter ID in tracker\n+\n+### Lifecycle — To Verify\n+\n+**`to_verify_at`** (timestamp, NULLABLE)\n+- **Purpose**: When the task was moved to verification/review state\n+- **Note**: NULL if task hasn't reached verification\n+- **Usage**: Development time (started → to_verify), review queue time\n+\n+**`to_verify_by_name`** (text, NULLABLE)\n+- **Purpose**: Who moved the task to verification\n+\n+**`to_verify_by_id`** (text, NULLABLE)\n+- **Purpose**: ID in tracker of the person who moved it to verification\n+\n+### Lifecycle — Done\n+\n+**`done_at`** (timestamp, NULLABLE)\n+- **Purpose**: When the task was completed\n+- **Note**: NULL if task is not done\n+- **Usage**: Verification time (to_verify → done), total cycle time (started → done)\n+\n+**`done_by_name`** (text, NULLABLE)\n+- **Purpose**: Who completed/verified the task\n+\n+**`done_by_id`** (text, NULLABLE)\n+- **Purpose**: Completer ID in tracker\n+\n+### System Fields\n+\n+**`ingestion_date`** (timestamp, NOT NULL)\n+- **Purpose**: When the record was ingested\n+- **Usage**: Incremental sync\n+\n+**`deleted`** (boolean, NOT NULL, DEFAULT false)\n+- **Purpose**: Soft delete flag\n+\n+**`metadata`** (jsonb, NULLABLE)\n+- **Purpose**: Source-specific fields\n+- **Examples**: `{\"resolution\": \"Fixed\", \"branch\": \"feature/MON-305\", \"spent_time\": \"4h\"}`\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Relationships\n+\n+### Parent\n+\n+**`user_story`**\n+- **Join**: `user_story_id` ← `task_id`\n+- **Cardinality**: Many tasks to one user story\n+- **Description**: Parent story this task implements\n+\n+### Cross-Stream\n+\n+- **Git commits**: `task_id` matches `raw_git.git_commit.task_id` — directly links tasks to code changes\n+- **Communication**: Correlate task activity with `stream_communication` events via assignee email\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Usage Examples\n+\n+### Task cycle time breakdown\n+\n+```sql\n+SELECT\n+    task_id,\n+    summary,\n+    assignee_name,\n+    EXTRACT(EPOCH FROM (started_at - created_at)) / 3600 as lead_time_hours,\n+    EXTRACT(EPOCH FROM (to_verify_at - started_at)) / 3600 as dev_time_hours,\n+    EXTRACT(EPOCH FROM (done_at - to_verify_at)) / 3600 as verify_time_hours,\n+    EXTRACT(EPOCH FROM (done_at - created_at)) / 3600 as total_time_hours\n+FROM task\n+WHERE done_at IS NOT NULL\n+  AND deleted = false\n+  AND done_at >= '2026-01-01'\n+ORDER BY total_time_hours DESC;\n+```\n+\n+### Developer throughput\n+\n+```sql\n+SELECT\n+    assignee_name,\n+    COUNT(*) as tasks_completed,\n+    AVG(EXTRACT(EPOCH FROM (done_at - started_at)) / 3600) as avg_cycle_hours,\n+    SUM(estimation) as total_estimated_hours\n+FROM task\n+WHERE done_at IS NOT NULL\n+  AND started_at IS NOT NULL\n+  AND deleted = false\n+  AND done_at >= '2026-01-01'\n+GROUP BY assignee_name\n+ORDER BY tasks_completed DESC;\n+```\n+\n+### Tasks stuck in verification\n+\n+```sql\n+SELECT\n+    task_id,\n+    summary,\n+    assignee_name,\n+    to_verify_at,\n+    NOW() - to_verify_at as waiting_time\n+FROM task\n+WHERE to_verify_at IS NOT NULL\n+  AND done_at IS NULL\n+  AND deleted = false\n+ORDER BY to_verify_at;\n+```\n+\n+### Tasks linked to commits\n+\n+```sql\n+SELECT\n+    t.task_id,\n+    t.summary,\n+    t.assignee_name,\n+    COUNT(c.id) as commit_count,\n+    SUM(ns.added) as lines_added,\n+    SUM(ns.removed) as lines_removed\n+FROM task t\n+JOIN raw_git.git_commit c ON t.task_id = c.task_id\n+LEFT JOIN raw_git.git_num_stat ns ON c.id = ns.commit_id\n+WHERE t.deleted = false\n+  AND t.done_at >= '2026-01-01'\n+GROUP BY t.task_id, t.summary, t.assignee_name\n+ORDER BY commit_count DESC\n+LIMIT 20;","path":"streams/stream_task_tracker/task.md","commit_id":"b079580cc3ce130cb78f98ecae10f237fb10b604","original_commit_id":"b079580cc3ce130cb78f98ecae10f237fb10b604","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**\"Tasks linked to commits\" silently excludes in-progress tasks via implicit NULL comparison.**\n\n`t.done_at >= '2026-01-01'` evaluates to NULL (excluded) for rows where `done_at IS NULL`. In-progress tasks with commits are invisibly dropped without any filter hint to the reader. Add an explicit `IS NOT NULL` guard or rename the query to clarify scope.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>🐛 Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n WHERE t.deleted = false\n-  AND t.done_at >= '2026-01-01'\n+  AND t.done_at IS NOT NULL\n+  AND t.done_at >= '2026-01-01'\n```\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Committable suggestion</summary>\n\n> ‼️ **IMPORTANT**\n> Carefully review the code before committing. Ensure that it accurately replaces the highlighted code, contains no missing lines, and has no issues with indentation. Thoroughly test & benchmark the code to ensure it meets the requirements.\n\n```suggestion\nJOIN raw_git.git_commit c ON t.task_id = c.task_id\nLEFT JOIN raw_git.git_num_stat ns ON c.id = ns.commit_id\nWHERE t.deleted = false\n  AND t.done_at IS NOT NULL\n  AND t.done_at >= '2026-01-01'\nGROUP BY t.task_id, t.summary, t.assignee_name\nORDER BY commit_count DESC\nLIMIT 20;\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_end -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@streams/stream_task_tracker/task.md` around lines 260 - 266, The WHERE clause\ncurrently uses \"t.done_at >= '2026-01-01'\" which implicitly excludes NULL\n(in-progress) tasks; update the query to make the intent explicit by adding \"AND\nt.done_at IS NOT NULL\" if you mean to only include completed tasks, or change\nthe predicate (e.g., remove the date comparison or add an OR condition) if you\nintend to include in-progress tasks with commits; reference the task\nalias/column (t.done_at) in the fix so the filter is unambiguous.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:triton:churro -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-02-23T10:41:20Z","updated_at":"2026-02-23T10:41:21Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/3#discussion_r2840140390","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/3","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/2840140390"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/3#discussion_r2840140390"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/3"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/2840140390/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":260,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":266,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"NONE","original_position":266,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/2840140398","pull_request_review_id":3840288777,"id":2840140398,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDORRWv8s6pSRpu","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,339 @@\n+# Table: `task`\n+\n+## Overview\n+\n+**Purpose**: Store individual task/sub-task work items with lifecycle timestamps and authorship. Tasks represent the smallest actionable units of work, typically implementing part of a user story.\n+\n+**Data Sources**:\n+- YouTrack: `source = \"youtrack\"`\n+- Jira: `source = \"jira\"`\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Schema Definition\n+\n+| Column | Type | Constraints | Description |\n+|--------|------|-------------|-------------|\n+| `id` | bigint | PRIMARY KEY, AUTO INCREMENT | Internal primary key |\n+| `ingestion_date` | timestamp | NOT NULL | When this record was ingested |\n+| `source` | text | NOT NULL | Source tracker: \"youtrack\" or \"jira\" |\n+| `source_id` | text | NOT NULL | Identifier in source tracker system |\n+| `task_id` | text | NOT NULL | Human-readable task ID (e.g., \"MON-305\") |\n+| `user_story_id` | text | NULLABLE | Parent user story ID (e.g., \"MON-201\") |\n+| `deleted` | boolean | NOT NULL, DEFAULT false | Soft delete flag |\n+| `summary` | text | NOT NULL | Task title/summary |\n+| `project` | text | NULLABLE | Project key |\n+| `priority` | text | NULLABLE | Priority level |\n+| `estimation` | numeric | NULLABLE | Time estimation (hours) |\n+| `sprint` | text | NULLABLE | Current sprint name |\n+| `assignee_name` | text | NULLABLE | Current assignee name |\n+| `assignee_id` | text | NULLABLE | Current assignee ID in tracker |\n+| `labels` | text[] | NULLABLE | Labels/tags |\n+| `created_at` | timestamp | NOT NULL | Task creation datetime |\n+| `created_by_name` | text | NOT NULL | Creator name |\n+| `created_by_id` | text | NOT NULL | Creator ID in tracker |\n+| `started_at` | timestamp | NULLABLE | When work on the task began |\n+| `started_by_name` | text | NULLABLE | Who started the task |\n+| `started_by_id` | text | NULLABLE | Starter ID in tracker |\n+| `to_verify_at` | timestamp | NULLABLE | When task was moved to verification |\n+| `to_verify_by_name` | text | NULLABLE | Who moved it to verification |\n+| `to_verify_by_id` | text | NULLABLE | Verifier-mover ID in tracker |\n+| `done_at` | timestamp | NULLABLE | Task completion datetime |\n+| `done_by_name` | text | NULLABLE | Who completed the task |\n+| `done_by_id` | text | NULLABLE | Completer ID in tracker |\n+| `metadata` | jsonb | NULLABLE | Source-specific additional data |\n+\n+**Indexes**:\n+- `idx_task_ingestion_date`: `(ingestion_date)` — incremental sync\n+- `idx_task_task_id`: `(task_id)`\n+- `idx_task_user_story_id`: `(user_story_id)` — parent story lookup\n+- `idx_task_project`: `(project)`\n+- `idx_task_sprint`: `(sprint)`\n+- `idx_task_assignee_id`: `(assignee_id)` — workload queries\n+- `idx_task_created_at`: `(created_at)`\n+- `idx_task_done_at`: `(done_at)`\n+- `(source, source_id)` — UNIQUE, prevents duplicates\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Field Semantics\n+\n+### Core Identifiers\n+\n+**`id`** (bigint, PRIMARY KEY)\n+- **Purpose**: Internal auto-increment key\n+\n+**`source`** (text, NOT NULL)\n+- **Purpose**: Identifies the source tracker system\n+- **Values**: \"youtrack\", \"jira\"\n+\n+**`source_id`** (text, NOT NULL)\n+- **Purpose**: Identifier in the source tracker system\n+- **Usage**: Trace back to source, deduplication\n+\n+**`task_id`** (text, NOT NULL)\n+- **Purpose**: Human-readable task identifier\n+- **Format**: \"PROJECT-NUMBER\" (e.g., \"MON-305\")\n+- **Usage**: Display, cross-referencing with commit messages\n+\n+**`user_story_id`** (text, NULLABLE)\n+- **Purpose**: Human-readable ID of the parent user story\n+- **Format**: \"PROJECT-NUMBER\" (e.g., \"MON-201\")\n+- **Note**: NULL if task is standalone (not linked to a story)\n+- **Usage**: Story→task hierarchy, rollup metrics\n+\n+### Task Details\n+\n+**`summary`** (text, NOT NULL)\n+- **Purpose**: Task title/summary\n+- **Examples**: \"Fix login timeout bug\", \"Add email validation\"\n+\n+**`project`** (text, NULLABLE)\n+- **Purpose**: Project key\n+- **Examples**: \"MON\", \"PLAT\"\n+\n+**`priority`** (text, NULLABLE)\n+- **Purpose**: Priority level\n+- **Examples**: \"Critical\", \"Major\", \"Normal\", \"Minor\"\n+\n+**`estimation`** (numeric, NULLABLE)\n+- **Purpose**: Estimated effort in hours\n+- **Examples**: 2, 4, 8, 16\n+- **Usage**: Estimation accuracy analysis, capacity planning\n+\n+**`sprint`** (text, NULLABLE)\n+- **Purpose**: Current or last sprint\n+- **Examples**: \"Sprint 24.1\", \"2026-W08\"\n+\n+**`assignee_name`** / **`assignee_id`** (text, NULLABLE)\n+- **Purpose**: Current assignee\n+- **Usage**: Workload analysis, developer metrics\n+\n+**`labels`** (text[], NULLABLE)\n+- **Purpose**: Labels/tags\n+\n+### Lifecycle — Creation\n+\n+**`created_at`** (timestamp, NOT NULL)\n+- **Purpose**: When the task was created\n+\n+**`created_by_name`** (text, NOT NULL)\n+- **Purpose**: Creator name\n+\n+**`created_by_id`** (text, NOT NULL)\n+- **Purpose**: Creator ID in tracker\n+\n+### Lifecycle — Started (In Progress)\n+\n+**`started_at`** (timestamp, NULLABLE)\n+- **Purpose**: When work on the task began (moved to \"In Progress\")\n+- **Note**: NULL if task hasn't been started\n+- **Usage**: Lead time (created → started), reaction time\n+\n+**`started_by_name`** (text, NULLABLE)\n+- **Purpose**: Who started working on the task\n+\n+**`started_by_id`** (text, NULLABLE)\n+- **Purpose**: Starter ID in tracker\n+\n+### Lifecycle — To Verify\n+\n+**`to_verify_at`** (timestamp, NULLABLE)\n+- **Purpose**: When the task was moved to verification/review state\n+- **Note**: NULL if task hasn't reached verification\n+- **Usage**: Development time (started → to_verify), review queue time\n+\n+**`to_verify_by_name`** (text, NULLABLE)\n+- **Purpose**: Who moved the task to verification\n+\n+**`to_verify_by_id`** (text, NULLABLE)\n+- **Purpose**: ID in tracker of the person who moved it to verification\n+\n+### Lifecycle — Done\n+\n+**`done_at`** (timestamp, NULLABLE)\n+- **Purpose**: When the task was completed\n+- **Note**: NULL if task is not done\n+- **Usage**: Verification time (to_verify → done), total cycle time (started → done)\n+\n+**`done_by_name`** (text, NULLABLE)\n+- **Purpose**: Who completed/verified the task\n+\n+**`done_by_id`** (text, NULLABLE)\n+- **Purpose**: Completer ID in tracker\n+\n+### System Fields\n+\n+**`ingestion_date`** (timestamp, NOT NULL)\n+- **Purpose**: When the record was ingested\n+- **Usage**: Incremental sync\n+\n+**`deleted`** (boolean, NOT NULL, DEFAULT false)\n+- **Purpose**: Soft delete flag\n+\n+**`metadata`** (jsonb, NULLABLE)\n+- **Purpose**: Source-specific fields\n+- **Examples**: `{\"resolution\": \"Fixed\", \"branch\": \"feature/MON-305\", \"spent_time\": \"4h\"}`\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Relationships\n+\n+### Parent\n+\n+**`user_story`**\n+- **Join**: `user_story_id` ← `task_id`\n+- **Cardinality**: Many tasks to one user story\n+- **Description**: Parent story this task implements\n+\n+### Cross-Stream\n+\n+- **Git commits**: `task_id` matches `raw_git.git_commit.task_id` — directly links tasks to code changes\n+- **Communication**: Correlate task activity with `stream_communication` events via assignee email\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Usage Examples\n+\n+### Task cycle time breakdown\n+\n+```sql\n+SELECT\n+    task_id,\n+    summary,\n+    assignee_name,\n+    EXTRACT(EPOCH FROM (started_at - created_at)) / 3600 as lead_time_hours,\n+    EXTRACT(EPOCH FROM (to_verify_at - started_at)) / 3600 as dev_time_hours,\n+    EXTRACT(EPOCH FROM (done_at - to_verify_at)) / 3600 as verify_time_hours,\n+    EXTRACT(EPOCH FROM (done_at - created_at)) / 3600 as total_time_hours\n+FROM task\n+WHERE done_at IS NOT NULL\n+  AND deleted = false\n+  AND done_at >= '2026-01-01'\n+ORDER BY total_time_hours DESC;\n+```\n+\n+### Developer throughput\n+\n+```sql\n+SELECT\n+    assignee_name,\n+    COUNT(*) as tasks_completed,\n+    AVG(EXTRACT(EPOCH FROM (done_at - started_at)) / 3600) as avg_cycle_hours,\n+    SUM(estimation) as total_estimated_hours\n+FROM task\n+WHERE done_at IS NOT NULL\n+  AND started_at IS NOT NULL\n+  AND deleted = false\n+  AND done_at >= '2026-01-01'\n+GROUP BY assignee_name\n+ORDER BY tasks_completed DESC;\n+```\n+\n+### Tasks stuck in verification\n+\n+```sql\n+SELECT\n+    task_id,\n+    summary,\n+    assignee_name,\n+    to_verify_at,\n+    NOW() - to_verify_at as waiting_time\n+FROM task\n+WHERE to_verify_at IS NOT NULL\n+  AND done_at IS NULL\n+  AND deleted = false\n+ORDER BY to_verify_at;\n+```\n+\n+### Tasks linked to commits\n+\n+```sql\n+SELECT\n+    t.task_id,\n+    t.summary,\n+    t.assignee_name,\n+    COUNT(c.id) as commit_count,\n+    SUM(ns.added) as lines_added,\n+    SUM(ns.removed) as lines_removed\n+FROM task t\n+JOIN raw_git.git_commit c ON t.task_id = c.task_id\n+LEFT JOIN raw_git.git_num_stat ns ON c.id = ns.commit_id\n+WHERE t.deleted = false\n+  AND t.done_at >= '2026-01-01'\n+GROUP BY t.task_id, t.summary, t.assignee_name\n+ORDER BY commit_count DESC\n+LIMIT 20;\n+```\n+\n+### Estimation accuracy\n+\n+```sql\n+SELECT\n+    assignee_name,\n+    COUNT(*) as tasks,\n+    AVG(estimation) as avg_estimated_hours,\n+    AVG(EXTRACT(EPOCH FROM (done_at - started_at)) / 3600) as avg_actual_hours,\n+    ROUND(AVG(EXTRACT(EPOCH FROM (done_at - started_at)) / 3600) /\n+          NULLIF(AVG(estimation), 0), 2) as actual_to_estimated_ratio\n+FROM task\n+WHERE done_at IS NOT NULL\n+  AND started_at IS NOT NULL\n+  AND estimation IS NOT NULL\n+  AND estimation > 0\n+  AND deleted = false\n+GROUP BY assignee_name\n+HAVING COUNT(*) >= 5\n+ORDER BY actual_to_estimated_ratio DESC;\n+```\n+\n+### Sprint completion report\n+\n+```sql\n+SELECT\n+    sprint,\n+    COUNT(*) as total_tasks,\n+    COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE done_at IS NOT NULL) as completed,\n+    COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE done_at IS NULL AND started_at IS NOT NULL) as in_progress,\n+    COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE started_at IS NULL) as not_started,","path":"streams/stream_task_tracker/task.md","commit_id":"b079580cc3ce130cb78f98ecae10f237fb10b604","original_commit_id":"b079580cc3ce130cb78f98ecae10f237fb10b604","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**`not_started` bucket double-counts tasks that skipped the \"started\" state.**\n\n`COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE started_at IS NULL)` includes tasks where `started_at IS NULL AND done_at IS NOT NULL` (tasks that jumped straight to done). The same tasks are already counted by the `completed` bucket, so `completed + in_progress + not_started` can exceed `total_tasks`, and `completion_pct` will appear to undercount.\n\nThe [Notes section explicitly acknowledges skipped states](`#skipped-states`), making this a real path.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>🐛 Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-    COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE started_at IS NULL) as not_started,\n+    COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE started_at IS NULL AND done_at IS NULL) as not_started,\n```\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Committable suggestion</summary>\n\n> ‼️ **IMPORTANT**\n> Carefully review the code before committing. Ensure that it accurately replaces the highlighted code, contains no missing lines, and has no issues with indentation. Thoroughly test & benchmark the code to ensure it meets the requirements.\n\n```suggestion\n    COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE done_at IS NOT NULL) as completed,\n    COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE done_at IS NULL AND started_at IS NOT NULL) as in_progress,\n    COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE started_at IS NULL AND done_at IS NULL) as not_started,\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_end -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@streams/stream_task_tracker/task.md` around lines 296 - 298, The not_started\nbucket currently counts rows with started_at IS NULL even if done_at IS NOT\nNULL, double-counting tasks that skipped straight to done; modify the\nnot_started FILTER to require both started_at IS NULL AND done_at IS NULL (i.e.,\nCOUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE started_at IS NULL AND done_at IS NULL) AS not_started)\nso skipped-to-done tasks remain only in the completed bucket and the three\nbuckets sum to total_tasks; update any dependent metrics (e.g., completion_pct)\nif they assume the old semantics.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:triton:churro -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-02-23T10:41:20Z","updated_at":"2026-02-23T10:41:22Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/3#discussion_r2840140398","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/3","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/2840140398"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pull/3#discussion_r2840140398"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/3"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/2840140398/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":296,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":298,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"NONE","original_position":298,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyber-insight/pulls/comments/2858731820","pull_request_review_id":3860587738,"id":2858731820,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDORRWv8s6qZMks","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,22 @@\n+\n+| id  | event_date | event_author | activity_ref | task_id | issue_ref | type      | created_date | done_date | state       | parent_issue_ref | assignee | title_version | description version | fields_map | fields_map                 | fields_map                   | fields_map      |","path":"streams/stream_task_tracker/table_example.md","commit_id":"7b4811e24e84830df73aabdea58e332784a65b32","original_commit_id":"81dc8a7b1b188af1a8973df750823b68fb578879","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html