like text\nor plaintext (e.g., change ``` to ```text) so syntax highlighting/rendering\ntreats it as plain text.\n````\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>streams/stream_task_tracker/table_example.md (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`5-20`: **Consider using ISO date format for consistency.**\n\nThe example uses date format \"1.01.26\", \"2.01.26\", etc., while the schema documentation specifies ISO format \"2026-01-02\" (line 64 in task_tracker_activities.md). Using consistent ISO format would improve clarity and match the schema specification.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>📅 Example with ISO dates</summary>\n\n```diff\n-| 1   | 1.01.26    | PM 1         | 2-0          | TASK-1  | 1-1       | User Story | 1.01.26      |           | new         |                  | PM 1     | 0             | 0                   |            | low                        |                              | no requirements |\n+| 1   | 2026-01-01 | PM 1         | 2-0          | TASK-1  | 1-1       | User Story | 2026-01-01   |           | new         |                  | PM 1     | 0             | 0                   |            | low                        |                              | no requirements |\n```\n\nApply similar conversion to all date fields in remaining rows.\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@streams/stream_task_tracker/table_example.md` around lines 5 - 20, The table\nuses non-ISO dates like \"1.01.26\", \"2.01.26\" etc., which conflicts with the\nschema in task_tracker_activities.md that expects ISO dates (e.g.,\n\"2026-01-02\"); update all date fields in\nstreams/stream_task_tracker/table_example.md to ISO 4‑digit year YYYY-MM-DD\nformat (for example convert \"1.01.26\" -> \"2026-01-01\", \"2.01.26\" ->\n\"2026-01-02\") so every date cell matches the documented schema and remain\nconsistent across the example rows.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for all review comments with AI agents</summary>\n\n````\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nInline comments:\nIn `@streams/stream_task_tracker/table_example.md`:\n- Line 2: The table header in table_example.md uses \"description version\" which\ndoesn't match the schema field name; update the header to \"description_version\"\nto match the definition in task_tracker_activities.md and ensure consistency\nwith other column names (e.g., id, event_date, title_version) so downstream\nparsing and docs remain aligned.\n- Around line 5-20: Replace the repeated typo \"User Stoy\" with \"User Story\" in\nthe table rows that contain that value (rows 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 11, 15, 16) so the\nissue type matches the schema; update the cell text exactly (maintain existing\nspacing/formatting in the Markdown row) in the table_example.md content where\nthe \"User Stoy\" string appears.\n\nIn `@streams/stream_task_tracker/task_tracker_activities.md`:\n- Line 19: Update the table row for the `source` field to use the proper\nplatform capitalization: change the example value `github` to `GitHub` so the\nTask tracker type list reads `youtrack`, `jira`, `GitHub`; ensure the\nbacktick-wrapped value is updated wherever the same `source` list is defined.\n\n---\n\nNitpick comments:\nIn `@streams/stream_task_tracker/table_example.md`:\n- Around line 5-20: The table uses non-ISO dates like \"1.01.26\", \"2.01.26\" etc.,\nwhich conflicts with the schema in task_tracker_activities.md that expects ISO\ndates (e.g., \"2026-01-02\"); update all date fields in\nstreams/stream_task_tracker/table_example.md to ISO 4‑digit year YYYY-MM-DD\nformat (for example convert \"1.01.26\" -> \"2026-01-01\", \"2.01.26\" ->\n\"2026-01-02\") so every date cell matches the documented schema and remain\nconsistent across the example rows.\n\nIn `@streams/stream_task_tracker/task_tracker_activit