pdated_at":"2026-03-05T09:24:18Z","body":"<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: summarize by coderabbit.ai -->\n<!-- walkthrough_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Walkthrough</summary>\n\n## Walkthrough\n\nFive comprehensive architecture documentation files are added covering the Insight platform's design, including connector integration patterns, identity resolution mechanisms, storage technology evaluation, product specification, and an example identity pipeline implementation.\n\n## Changes\n\n| Cohort / File(s) | Summary |\n|---|---|\n| **Core Platform Architecture** <br> `docs/architecture/PRODUCT_SPECIFICATION.md`, `docs/architecture/STORAGE_TECHNOLOGY_EVALUATION.md` | High-level platform architecture specification detailing two-layer design (Metrics and Analytics), deployment phases, user segments, and comprehensive storage technology evaluation with decision rationale comparing ClickHouse, MariaDB ColumnStore, and PostgreSQL + TimescaleDB. |\n| **Identity Resolution Framework** <br> `docs/architecture/IDENTITY_RESOLUTION_V2.md`, `docs/architecture/EXAMPLE_IDENTITY_PIPELINE.md` | Complete identity resolution architecture v2 with dual-database design (MariaDB InnoDB + ClickHouse), two-phase resolution flow, rule-based matching, and a Bronze-to-Gold medallion layer example pipeline with source integration and attribute conflict handling. |\n| **Connector Integration** <br> `docs/architecture/CONNECTORS_ARCHITECTURE.md` | Multi-layer connector architecture documentation including standardized Connector Contract specification, Unifier Schemas with semantic metadata, data flow patterns (API, file, webhook-based), implementation guidelines, and semantic propagation rules to Analytics Layer. |\n\n## Estimated code review effort\n\n🎯 4 (Complex) | ⏱️ ~55 minutes\n\n## Possibly related PRs\n\n- **cyberfabric/insight-spec#4**: Refines connector and unifier documentation alongside Silver→Gold identity-resolved ingestion patterns, including semantic naming conventions and identity resolution integration details.\n\n## Poem\n\n> 🐰 *Hopping through layers, from Bronze to Gold we bound,*  \n> *Connectors unify what once was scattered 'round,*  \n> *Identities resolve where MariaDB and Click align,*  \n> *Architecture maps the Metrics path so fine,*  \n> *With whiskers twitching at this spec so bright,*  \n> *We celebrate foundations, documented right!* ✨\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- walkthrough_end -->\n\n\n<!-- pre_merge_checks_walkthrough_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>🚥 Pre-merge checks | ✅ 3</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>✅ Passed checks (3 passed)</summary>\n\n|     Check name     | Status   | Explanation                                                                                                                                                                                               |\n| :----------------: | :------- | :-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n|  Description Check | ✅ Passed | Check skipped - CodeRabbit’s high-level summary is enabled.                                                                                                                                               |\n|     Title check    | ✅ Passed | The PR title accurately captures the main focus of the changeset, which centers on Identity Resolution architecture and conceptual ETL/data flow patterns documented across multiple specification files. |\n| Docstring Coverage | ✅ Passed | No functions found in the changed files to evaluate docstring coverage. Skipping docstring coverage check.                                                                                                |\n\n</details>\n\n<sub>✏️ Tip: You can configure your own custom pre-merge checks in the settings.</sub>\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- pre_merge_checks_walkthrough_end -->\n\n<!-- finishing_touch_checkbox_start 